1
00:00:29,946 --> 00:00:31,197
‪Wow, there's meat in here.

2
00:00:31,281 --> 00:00:33,283
‪It's been forever since I've had some.

3
00:00:37,454 --> 00:00:38,830
‪I'm so exhausted.

4
00:00:40,498 --> 00:00:41,624
‪I have to win.

5
00:00:42,834 --> 00:00:43,877
‪Winning is the goal.

6
00:00:44,669 --> 00:00:46,129
‪I've been thinking.

7
00:00:46,713 --> 00:00:49,382
‪About the hidden quest.

8
00:00:49,466 --> 00:00:51,301
‪-When it comes down to it,
‪-Yeah?

9
00:00:51,384 --> 00:00:53,344
‪I went in there completely blind,

10
00:00:53,428 --> 00:00:56,014
‪-and what I earned was out of sheer luck.
‪-Right.

11
00:00:56,097 --> 00:00:57,849
‪You were the one who figured out

12
00:00:57,932 --> 00:01:00,810
‪-the cast puzzle portion of it.
‪-Yeah.

13
00:01:01,895 --> 00:01:03,313
‪And I believe…

14
00:01:04,314 --> 00:01:05,398
‪that's a notable contribution.

15
00:01:05,982 --> 00:01:10,070
‪If you're intent on going all the way,

16
00:01:10,153 --> 00:01:12,363
‪I can promise to save this token

17
00:01:12,447 --> 00:01:15,825
‪so I can use it on you or me
‪when the time comes.

18
00:01:15,909 --> 00:01:19,162
‪Jung Won-young,
‪since you succeeded in breaking the curse,

19
00:01:19,245 --> 00:01:21,039
‪you will receive the salvation token.

20
00:01:21,122 --> 00:01:24,417
‪It is usable through the end
‪of the fifth main match

21
00:01:24,501 --> 00:01:28,213
‪and can be transferred to another player.

22
00:01:28,296 --> 00:01:31,466
‪Honestly, for today's main match,

23
00:01:31,549 --> 00:01:36,638
‪I'm thinking of playing for my advantage
‪rather than yesterday's allegiance.

24
00:01:36,721 --> 00:01:39,098
<i>‪I honestly believe Dong-jae</i>

25
00:01:39,182 --> 00:01:42,977
<i>‪has proven his capabilities and potential</i>
<i>‪to be an all-around player.</i>

26
00:01:43,061 --> 00:01:46,231
<i>‪In the first counting mini-game</i>
<i>‪determining the priority ranking,</i>

27
00:01:46,314 --> 00:01:47,649
<i>‪he took the first spot.</i>

28
00:01:47,732 --> 00:01:51,069
‪So, following the Jang-Oh Alliance,

29
00:01:51,653 --> 00:01:54,072
‪I'm gonna attempt to create
‪the Young-Jae Alliance.

30
00:01:54,155 --> 00:01:57,325
‪Before you even brought this up,

31
00:01:57,909 --> 00:01:59,035
‪I meant to ask you

32
00:02:00,245 --> 00:02:02,205
‪if you're interested
‪in teaming up with me.

33
00:02:02,997 --> 00:02:04,666
‪At the end of the day,

34
00:02:04,749 --> 00:02:08,044
‪there can only be one winner
‪in this competition.

35
00:02:08,128 --> 00:02:11,965
‪It's not like I promised Dong-min forever.

36
00:02:13,299 --> 00:02:15,760
‪-Good morning.
‪-Hey.

37
00:02:20,723 --> 00:02:22,559
‪Let's talk again later.

38
00:02:23,726 --> 00:02:25,186
‪It's the same thing.

39
00:02:25,270 --> 00:02:29,440
‪I can never fully trust him,
‪since he has a history of lying.

40
00:02:29,524 --> 00:02:32,694
<i>‪Won-young went into that secret room,</i>
<i>‪saw the message,</i>

41
00:02:32,777 --> 00:02:34,696
<i>‪and got the reward by himself.</i>

42
00:02:34,779 --> 00:02:37,782
<i>‪We have no way of confirming any of it.</i>

43
00:02:37,866 --> 00:02:42,078
‪But yesterday,
‪XITSUH volunteered for the prison match.

44
00:02:42,162 --> 00:02:45,915
<i>‪That has to weigh on Dong-min,</i>

45
00:02:45,999 --> 00:02:48,835
<i>‪and if it does, I'm the one in trouble.</i>

46
00:02:48,918 --> 00:02:54,757
<i>‪So I wanna lock in a reliable ally now,</i>
<i>‪while I still can.</i>

47
00:02:54,841 --> 00:02:57,260
<i>‪I think I'll end up </i><i>‪joining </i><i>‪forces</i>
<i>‪with Won-young.</i>

48
00:03:01,806 --> 00:03:03,099
‪The breakfast is good today.

49
00:03:21,826 --> 00:03:23,578
‪I'm done.

50
00:03:23,661 --> 00:03:24,746
‪-You are?
‪-Yes.

51
00:03:25,246 --> 00:03:26,456
‪I don't have much of an appetite.

52
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:32,503
‪I wonder if our dear Won-young

53
00:03:32,587 --> 00:03:36,215
‪decided to team up
‪with Dong-min again or not.

54
00:03:36,299 --> 00:03:38,801
‪I'd look pretty dumb if he did.

55
00:03:38,885 --> 00:03:40,053
‪What?

56
00:03:40,136 --> 00:03:42,639
‪If they say
‪their roster's already full, then…

57
00:03:43,806 --> 00:03:45,975
‪I'm fine going in with a grudge
‪and seeking revenge.

58
00:03:46,059 --> 00:03:48,436
‪Why wouldn't you play with them?

59
00:03:48,519 --> 00:03:51,648
‪Numbers are tight today.

60
00:03:51,731 --> 00:03:54,984
‪Dong-jae, Yurisa, me,

61
00:03:55,068 --> 00:03:56,110
‪plus Dong-min make four.

62
00:03:56,194 --> 00:03:57,779
‪That math doesn't add up.

63
00:03:58,363 --> 00:04:00,323
‪-Something has to give.
‪-Right.

64
00:04:04,369 --> 00:04:07,121
‪Do you think we'll go with the same teams
‪if it's a four-on-three game today?

65
00:04:07,205 --> 00:04:09,707
‪If Won-young's been recruited…

66
00:04:09,791 --> 00:04:12,043
‪Then there's not much we can do.

67
00:04:12,126 --> 00:04:15,630
‪I'm just focused
‪on avoiding last place right now.

68
00:04:16,339 --> 00:04:19,050
‪I just need to make sure
‪someone up there comes in last place.

69
00:04:19,133 --> 00:04:21,469
‪Then I can just play the prison match.

70
00:04:21,552 --> 00:04:23,846
‪That's been my mindset
‪for about two days now.

71
00:04:23,930 --> 00:04:26,266
‪I think that comes naturally
‪if you're here long enough.

72
00:04:26,349 --> 00:04:28,935
‪I'm confident I can handle
‪any prison match.

73
00:04:29,018 --> 00:04:34,774
‪I'm the only one here who's been in prison
‪since the first day.

74
00:04:34,857 --> 00:04:37,443
<i>‪I'm not scared</i>
<i>‪about coming back to prison at all.</i>

75
00:04:37,527 --> 00:04:40,071
<i>‪I just need to make sure</i>
<i>‪I don't lose and get eliminated.</i>

76
00:04:40,154 --> 00:04:42,323
<i>‪Then I can play another game</i>

77
00:04:42,407 --> 00:04:45,326
‪and survive another day.

78
00:04:46,995 --> 00:04:48,663
‪-Good luck!
‪-You got this!

79
00:04:50,957 --> 00:04:52,333
‪Oh my gosh! He's gone!

80
00:04:53,084 --> 00:04:55,086
‪He's really gone.

81
00:04:55,169 --> 00:04:56,337
‪The sun's back.

82
00:04:57,046 --> 00:05:00,216
‪I wish it could open just one more time,
‪but the bird only calls out once a day.

83
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:02,552
‪Yeah, once every twelve hours
‪would be perfect.

84
00:05:03,761 --> 00:05:04,679
‪I know, right?

85
00:05:04,762 --> 00:05:09,183
‪We have to get through another match
‪just to get a shot at it.

86
00:05:09,267 --> 00:05:13,438
‪I was so jealous because God's test
‪only takes place once a day.

87
00:05:13,521 --> 00:05:17,483
‪Missing that chance means
‪you end up in another exile zone match,

88
00:05:17,567 --> 00:05:20,737
‪and you have to survive that
‪to have another chance the following day.

89
00:05:20,820 --> 00:05:23,239
‪I cheered him on with all my heart
‪as he left.

90
00:05:23,323 --> 00:05:24,407
‪But secretly,

91
00:05:24,490 --> 00:05:26,159
‪I hoped he'd fail.

92
00:05:26,743 --> 00:05:27,952
‪I wonder what he's doing.

93
00:05:28,828 --> 00:05:29,912
‪Yeah.

94
00:05:29,996 --> 00:05:32,540
‪I hope he makes it and shocks everyone.

95
00:05:32,623 --> 00:05:35,335
‪Not me. I want one of us to do that.

96
00:05:37,211 --> 00:05:38,755
‪If multiple people could go…

97
00:05:38,838 --> 00:05:40,089
‪I know, right?

98
00:05:40,173 --> 00:05:42,300
‪-I would be genuinely cheering him on.
‪-Right.

99
00:05:43,885 --> 00:05:45,553
‪Do you think it'll close back up?

100
00:05:46,554 --> 00:05:49,057
‪-It's been about an hour now.
‪-Right.

101
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:51,225
‪I flipped it
‪the moment the lights went out.

102
00:05:52,393 --> 00:05:53,561
‪The 15-minute one?

103
00:05:53,644 --> 00:05:54,604
‪The one-hour one.

104
00:05:56,272 --> 00:05:57,940
‪I'm about to die of curiosity.

105
00:05:59,442 --> 00:06:01,736
‪What sort of battle
‪could he be facing right now?

106
00:06:01,819 --> 00:06:02,987
‪I have no idea.

107
00:06:03,071 --> 00:06:04,614
‪I really wanna know what time it is.

108
00:06:04,697 --> 00:06:05,948
‪I should bring it over.

109
00:06:12,038 --> 00:06:13,081
‪It's been an hour.

110
00:06:14,082 --> 00:06:15,333
‪Why aren't they announcing it?

111
00:06:15,416 --> 00:06:16,584
<i>‪Ha Seok-jin.</i>

112
00:06:18,586 --> 00:06:19,754
<i>‪Ha Seok-jin.</i>

113
00:06:22,131 --> 00:06:24,801
<i>‪You have failed God's test.</i>

114
00:06:28,805 --> 00:06:31,307
‪-I guess it's hard.
‪-It must be insanely difficult.

115
00:06:38,397 --> 00:06:41,526
‪Having tried it myself,
‪I can say an hour isn't enough time.

116
00:06:42,235 --> 00:06:45,238
‪And so, my journey comes to a close.

117
00:06:48,533 --> 00:06:50,368
<i>‪This show gave me glory</i>

118
00:06:50,451 --> 00:06:52,745
<i>‪and so much joy.</i>

119
00:06:52,829 --> 00:06:55,206
‪Out of gratitude for that experience,

120
00:06:55,289 --> 00:06:59,335
<i>‪I decided to take a second chance.</i>

121
00:06:59,418 --> 00:07:04,090
<i>‪The exiles worked together</i>
<i>‪to solve the puzzles</i>

122
00:07:04,173 --> 00:07:07,385
<i>‪and even managed to build</i>
<i>‪a magic square with small numbers.</i>

123
00:07:07,468 --> 00:07:12,140
<i>‪I think I've done my part</i>
<i>‪in </i><i>‪the </i><i>‪exile </i><i>‪zone, </i><i>‪in my own way.</i>

124
00:07:12,723 --> 00:07:14,142
‪Thank you.

125
00:07:14,851 --> 00:07:17,145
‪-I guess you get an hour to solve it?
‪-Yeah.

126
00:07:18,146 --> 00:07:21,315
‪As soon as they announced he failed,

127
00:07:21,399 --> 00:07:23,025
‪I realized I made the right decision
‪to come here.

128
00:07:23,109 --> 00:07:24,360
‪Unbelievable.

129
00:07:25,570 --> 00:07:27,196
‪The master of flip-flopping.

130
00:07:28,281 --> 00:07:30,324
‪-You have a chance now.
‪-Right.

131
00:07:30,408 --> 00:07:32,827
‪I'll give it my best shot.

132
00:07:32,910 --> 00:07:34,537
‪-Sure.
‪-What am I gonna do?

133
00:07:34,620 --> 00:07:36,372
‪It must be super hard.

134
00:07:36,456 --> 00:07:40,168
‪-You can totally say no.
‪-Okay.

135
00:07:40,751 --> 00:07:42,879
‪-Seok-jin just failed.
‪-Right.

136
00:07:42,962 --> 00:07:44,839
‪Do you think you can pull it off?

137
00:07:44,922 --> 00:07:46,132
‪-I'm just saying.
‪-I have to try.

138
00:07:46,215 --> 00:07:47,467
‪-If you're feeling unsure,
‪-Okay.

139
00:07:47,550 --> 00:07:51,637
‪I'll run through
‪every possible algorithm there is with you

140
00:07:51,721 --> 00:07:52,805
‪if you let me go first.

141
00:07:52,889 --> 00:07:53,973
‪No can do.

142
00:07:54,056 --> 00:07:56,392
‪-Because then you'd--
‪-I'd lose my chance, so no.

143
00:07:56,476 --> 00:07:59,770
‪-If it was too hard for him,
‪-Okay.

144
00:07:59,854 --> 00:08:03,065
‪there's a high chance you'd fail as well,
‪even if it were the same game.

145
00:08:03,149 --> 00:08:08,196
‪But I know all the odd numbers
‪and everything.

146
00:08:08,279 --> 00:08:11,657
‪But attempting it is different
‪from not attempting it at all.

147
00:08:11,741 --> 00:08:12,700
‪-So if I--
‪-Look.

148
00:08:12,783 --> 00:08:16,204
‪If I let you go first,
‪I'd be stuck here until the final match.

149
00:08:16,287 --> 00:08:18,331
‪That wouldn't make any sense for me.

150
00:08:18,414 --> 00:08:21,959
‪Right, that's why I said earlier
‪that you can just say no.

151
00:08:22,043 --> 00:08:25,004
‪-I just wanna get it over with.
‪-Okay, got it.

152
00:08:25,087 --> 00:08:26,797
‪I don't wanna be here
‪until the sixth day either.

153
00:08:26,881 --> 00:08:27,965
‪Understood.

154
00:08:28,049 --> 00:08:29,467
‪Sorry, but I'm going for it.

155
00:08:29,550 --> 00:08:31,135
‪I'm more impatient, if anything.

156
00:08:31,219 --> 00:08:32,845
‪Understood.

157
00:08:33,429 --> 00:08:36,682
‪You're so funny,
‪trying to be sneaky and cut the line.

158
00:08:38,059 --> 00:08:40,311
‪Should we flip that back over?

159
00:08:40,811 --> 00:08:42,021
‪-That?
‪-Yes.

160
00:08:45,733 --> 00:08:47,109
‪-Should we?
‪-What?

161
00:08:47,193 --> 00:08:48,152
‪Should we mess it up?

162
00:08:48,236 --> 00:08:50,071
‪Flip it over? Wait, mess it up?

163
00:08:50,947 --> 00:08:52,865
‪-I'm a little worried though.
‪-Okay.

164
00:08:52,949 --> 00:08:57,370
‪I was able to step aside
‪because if you failed,

165
00:08:57,453 --> 00:09:00,206
‪there'd be enough time
‪for me to get a chance.

166
00:09:00,289 --> 00:09:01,958
‪But when the next person realizes

167
00:09:02,041 --> 00:09:04,710
‪they won't get a chance
‪based on the current order,

168
00:09:04,794 --> 00:09:06,671
‪they might not like it

169
00:09:06,754 --> 00:09:08,464
‪and suggest a game to switch it up.

170
00:09:08,548 --> 00:09:13,010
‪I mean, I'll definitely
‪get my chance tomorrow.

171
00:09:13,094 --> 00:09:17,265
‪If you're feeling anxious about it,
‪you're free to flip them over.

172
00:09:17,348 --> 00:09:18,558
‪Okay.

173
00:09:18,641 --> 00:09:21,769
‪I won't disagree
‪because I can feel your desperation.

174
00:09:21,852 --> 00:09:22,812
‪Thank you.

175
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:32,780
‪You really took out every piece.

176
00:09:34,824 --> 00:09:37,702
‪I guess that's how you survive
‪in a survival show, huh?

177
00:09:40,371 --> 00:09:42,081
‪Why did he fail?

178
00:09:42,582 --> 00:09:44,458
‪He failed even after working on it
‪for an hour?

179
00:09:45,042 --> 00:09:47,503
‪That's what the test is, right?

180
00:09:47,587 --> 00:09:50,590
‪So it's just a matter of
‪what variation of it we get.

181
00:09:51,465 --> 00:09:53,509
‪This is already a seven-by-seven.

182
00:09:53,593 --> 00:09:55,886
‪It must be even harder if he failed.

183
00:09:55,970 --> 00:09:58,347
‪Didn't he breeze through
‪the seven-by-seven and nine-by-nine?

184
00:09:58,431 --> 00:10:00,391
‪-You just need to know the trick.
‪-Right.

185
00:10:01,017 --> 00:10:02,727
‪Maybe he got stuck doing the 11-by-11.

186
00:10:02,810 --> 00:10:03,686
‪Maybe.

187
00:10:03,769 --> 00:10:05,521
‪When it's 11 by 11,

188
00:10:05,605 --> 00:10:07,732
‪just writing it all out
‪is a challenge in itself.

189
00:10:09,650 --> 00:10:11,235
‪-Oh, hey.
‪-Did it arrive?

190
00:10:11,319 --> 00:10:12,653
‪What is it?

191
00:10:13,195 --> 00:10:14,447
‪Peanuts and almonds.

192
00:10:15,031 --> 00:10:16,240
‪Amazing.

193
00:10:21,954 --> 00:10:23,456
‪-The almonds are so good.
‪-Yeah.

194
00:10:23,539 --> 00:10:26,751
<i>‪The almonds and peanuts</i>
<i>‪arrived just in time.</i>

195
00:10:26,834 --> 00:10:29,253
‪I can't believe
‪they held out on us like that.

196
00:10:29,337 --> 00:10:34,091
‪I used them to load up on calories
‪and practice the magic square.

197
00:10:39,847 --> 00:10:40,681
‪That's the stuff.

198
00:10:41,557 --> 00:10:43,184
‪What if it's not a magic square?

199
00:10:43,267 --> 00:10:45,853
‪I think it's guaranteed that it is
‪at this point.

200
00:10:46,520 --> 00:10:48,189
‪So it comes down
‪to the size of the board, huh?

201
00:10:50,399 --> 00:10:51,817
‪How are you marking them?

202
00:10:52,318 --> 00:10:54,153
‪I'm using almonds to stand in for five.

203
00:10:55,529 --> 00:10:57,198
‪Such a waste of good almonds.

204
00:10:57,281 --> 00:10:58,324
‪I know, right?

205
00:10:59,950 --> 00:11:01,118
‪Did you mess up?

206
00:11:01,202 --> 00:11:02,370
‪Do you need to redo it?

207
00:11:04,038 --> 00:11:05,665
‪-Are you close?
‪-Kind of?

208
00:11:06,874 --> 00:11:09,543
<i>‪Honestly, I'm a little hesitant</i>

209
00:11:09,627 --> 00:11:13,714
‪to share what I know
‪about how to solve this game.

210
00:11:13,798 --> 00:11:17,843
‪If JAE JAE also fails tomorrow,

211
00:11:17,927 --> 00:11:20,012
‪I'll get my shot.

212
00:11:20,096 --> 00:11:22,556
<i>‪I'm just living off that hope right now.</i>

213
00:11:22,640 --> 00:11:24,850
‪I wish whoever it is
‪would just get here already.

214
00:11:24,934 --> 00:11:26,936
‪I'm so curious
‪about what's happening back there.

215
00:11:27,019 --> 00:11:28,854
‪But if XITSUH comes, that's trouble.

216
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:31,023
‪-Dong-jae too.
‪-Why?

217
00:11:31,107 --> 00:11:32,483
‪Because I'll be crying nonstop.

218
00:11:34,735 --> 00:11:37,530
‪You call that trouble? Goodness gracious.

219
00:11:37,613 --> 00:11:39,865
‪-How ridiculous.
‪-It'll take me an hour to calm down.

220
00:11:39,949 --> 00:11:42,201
‪-So it'll be teary trouble?
‪-Yeah.

221
00:11:42,284 --> 00:11:44,203
‪If Dong-jae or XITSUH comes, that is.

222
00:11:44,870 --> 00:11:45,871
‪Out of joy?

223
00:11:46,414 --> 00:11:49,750
‪-You barely get time to say goodbye.
‪-Right, that's rough.

224
00:11:49,834 --> 00:11:50,751
‪That's why.

225
