‪-You can fully support us.
‪-Not interested in winning?

423
00:20:57,673 --> 00:20:58,882
‪-I'm not in it to win.
‪-Really?

424
00:20:58,966 --> 00:21:00,509
‪-I just--
‪-Then just focus on us.

425
00:21:00,592 --> 00:21:02,386
‪If ORBIT enters the bid with us,

426
00:21:02,469 --> 00:21:04,680
‪he could just bid one won
‪and let us win it.

427
00:21:04,763 --> 00:21:06,473
‪-We--
‪-That's one way.

428
00:21:06,556 --> 00:21:08,225
‪-He could also defend us.
‪-We just don't know yet.

429
00:21:08,308 --> 00:21:09,935
‪-Right.
‪-Who knows what will happen?

430
00:21:10,018 --> 00:21:12,980
‪Okay, let's first do the Piece count.

431
00:21:14,064 --> 00:21:15,357
‪-How many do you have?
‪-Two.

432
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:16,275
‪Two. What about you?

433
00:21:16,358 --> 00:21:17,401
‪-Two.
‪-Two.

434
00:21:17,484 --> 00:21:19,444
‪-I have one. How many do you have? Two?
‪-Two.

435
00:21:19,528 --> 00:21:20,612
‪-I have three.
‪-Three.

436
00:21:20,696 --> 00:21:21,738
‪-I also have three.
‪-Three.

437
00:21:21,822 --> 00:21:23,740
‪-Dong-min has five, right?
‪-Right.

438
00:21:24,283 --> 00:21:26,576
‪We have 12 total. That team has 9.

439
00:21:26,660 --> 00:21:28,120
‪We are at a disadvantage.

440
00:21:28,203 --> 00:21:31,331
‪They can use Pieces

441
00:21:31,415 --> 00:21:33,083
‪to outlast us across rounds.

442
00:21:33,166 --> 00:21:35,210
‪Three one-won coins,

443
00:21:35,794 --> 00:21:36,962
‪three two-won coins,

444
00:21:37,045 --> 00:21:38,380
‪two three-won coins,

445
00:21:38,463 --> 00:21:40,090
‪one five-won coin, and one ten-won coin.

446
00:21:40,173 --> 00:21:43,176
‪But they said we can break the coins.

447
00:21:43,260 --> 00:21:44,094
‪No, we can't.

448
00:21:44,177 --> 00:21:45,721
‪-Oh, we can't? I see.
‪-No.

449
00:21:45,804 --> 00:21:48,223
‪The star is really important
‪since it's in the center,

450
00:21:48,307 --> 00:21:49,933
‪but it's the fewest in number.

451
00:21:50,017 --> 00:21:54,563
‪Just looking at it now,
‪which shape looks best to you guys?

452
00:21:54,646 --> 00:21:57,566
‪Just going by the numbers,
‪probably the circle.

453
00:21:57,649 --> 00:21:59,901
‪-Right.
‪-It'll probably draw a lot of bids too.

454
00:21:59,985 --> 00:22:05,365
‪When our team needs to save coins,
‪we should back one person to win.

455
00:22:05,449 --> 00:22:08,410
‪Because the shape is awarded
‪based on the number of bidders

456
00:22:08,493 --> 00:22:11,079
‪divided by the number of winners.

457
00:22:11,163 --> 00:22:12,456
‪Two people can bid minimum

458
00:22:12,539 --> 00:22:14,833
‪and let the remaining one person
‪bid high and win three shapes

459
00:22:14,916 --> 00:22:15,834
‪on a throwaway round.

460
00:22:15,917 --> 00:22:17,544
‪-Say it's a throwaway round,
‪-We need to make a choice.

461
00:22:17,627 --> 00:22:18,503
‪and you put it one won.

462
00:22:18,587 --> 00:22:21,381
‪If we bid for the same shape,
‪I can win two of them.

463
00:22:21,465 --> 00:22:24,217
‪That team will probably do that
‪to make Dong-min win again today.

464
00:22:24,301 --> 00:22:26,803
‪But if it's four versus four,

465
00:22:26,887 --> 00:22:30,140
‪this really becomes an information war
‪plus an actual fair fight.

466
00:22:30,223 --> 00:22:32,517
‪Since our numbers are even now,

467
00:22:32,601 --> 00:22:34,352
‪we're in a really good place.

468
00:22:34,436 --> 00:22:36,646
‪There's no one here
‪with a connection to that team, right?

469
00:22:36,730 --> 00:22:38,607
‪I guess I have a small one.
‪I was in prison with them.

470
00:22:38,690 --> 00:22:42,027
‪-I mean, the living area.
‪-Then they'll see you as an ally here.

471
00:22:42,110 --> 00:22:43,195
‪They won't.

472
00:22:43,278 --> 00:22:44,404
‪They don't trust me.

473
00:22:44,488 --> 00:22:46,281
‪-Oh, they don't trust you?
‪-No.

474
00:22:47,282 --> 00:22:49,701
‪Tell us what you're thinking.

475
00:22:49,785 --> 00:22:53,622
‪-First, I think Dong-min…
‪-We must keep him in check.

476
00:22:54,206 --> 00:22:57,250
‪We have to keep our guard up
‪in any round Dong-min's involved in.

477
00:22:57,334 --> 00:23:01,713
‪Okay, so the four of us have to assume
‪they'll maximize his chances

478
00:23:01,797 --> 00:23:06,510
‪somehow and someway
‪and play it as safe as possible.

479
00:23:06,593 --> 00:23:08,553
‪Then we need to find an opening
‪somewhere in there.

480
00:23:08,637 --> 00:23:10,847
‪Is XITSUH showing any change of heart?

481
00:23:10,931 --> 00:23:13,892
‪Earlier, he…

482
00:23:13,975 --> 00:23:17,270
‪-We'll have to see how the game plays out,
‪-Yes?

483
00:23:17,354 --> 00:23:20,899
‪but if there's a surefire way
‪to take down a strong player,

484
00:23:21,525 --> 00:23:22,400
‪let's talk.

485
00:23:22,984 --> 00:23:23,902
‪You mean that?

486
00:23:23,985 --> 00:23:25,695
‪-You'd consider it?
‪-This is a survival show.

487
00:23:25,779 --> 00:23:27,614
‪If it's a 100% certainty, then yes.

488
00:23:28,615 --> 00:23:30,367
‪From a survival standpoint,

489
00:23:30,450 --> 00:23:32,953
‪the system is giving us an opportunity.

490
00:23:33,036 --> 00:23:35,288
‪He said he'd be open to working with us

491
00:23:35,372 --> 00:23:37,249
‪if we could make
‪a strong player place last.

492
00:23:37,874 --> 00:23:40,293
‪Right now, the only information available

493
00:23:40,377 --> 00:23:43,338
‪is how much someone's gonna bid.

494
00:23:43,421 --> 00:23:44,965
‪Either way, this is a mind game,

495
00:23:45,048 --> 00:23:49,261
‪and the highest winning bid
‪is kept secret,

496
00:23:49,344 --> 00:23:51,680
‪so we have to predict that too.

497
00:23:52,430 --> 00:23:54,391
‪But there's no way to know for sure.

498
00:23:54,975 --> 00:23:59,604
‪Right, that's something everyone
‪has to handle on their own today.

499
00:23:59,688 --> 00:24:01,731
‪Sharing information? Not today.

500
00:24:01,815 --> 00:24:04,734
‪You can't even share it
‪within your own team,

501
00:24:04,818 --> 00:24:06,862
‪so forget about gathering intel
‪from the opposing team.

502
00:24:06,945 --> 00:24:09,948
<i>‪It's an eight-person psychological battle,</i>
<i>‪fought individually.</i>

503
00:24:10,031 --> 00:24:12,284
<i>‪I can't fully trust</i>

504
00:24:12,367 --> 00:24:16,288
‪my own teammates this time either.

505
00:24:16,371 --> 00:24:18,999
<i>‪Even if we all agree</i>
<i>‪to bid one won together,</i>

506
00:24:20,542 --> 00:24:23,378
‪apart from XITSUH,

507
00:24:23,461 --> 00:24:25,297
<i>‪I suspect both Dong-jae and Yurisa</i>

508
00:24:25,380 --> 00:24:29,593
<i>‪are the type who could easily spend</i>
<i>‪two or three won to win.</i>

509
00:24:30,594 --> 00:24:34,055
‪This is a game where you can easily
‪target one player to eliminate them.

510
00:24:34,848 --> 00:24:36,391
‪That is, if enough people join forces.

511
00:24:36,474 --> 00:24:39,060
<i>‪A four-person team</i>
<i>‪doesn't even make sense today</i>

512
00:24:39,144 --> 00:24:41,188
<i>‪since only three</i>
<i>‪can go to the living area.</i>

513
00:24:41,271 --> 00:24:42,856
<i>‪I'm already sensing it today.</i>

514
00:24:42,939 --> 00:24:47,402
‪The whole "team" thing
‪isn't gonna last much longer.

515
00:24:48,236 --> 00:24:49,529
‪It's perfect timing.

516
00:24:50,822 --> 00:24:52,532
<i>‪Your time is up.</i>

517
00:24:52,616 --> 00:24:55,035
<i>‪Auction Bingo will now begin.</i>

518
00:24:55,785 --> 00:24:57,913
‪We'll now hand out your name tickets.

519
00:24:57,996 --> 00:24:59,247
‪Oh, these are cool.

520
00:24:59,331 --> 00:25:00,498
‪-Thank you.
‪-Yurisa.

521
00:25:00,582 --> 00:25:01,791
‪-Thank you. Wow.
‪-Wow.

522
00:25:01,875 --> 00:25:03,835
‪I should've taken a better photo.
‪I look so chubby.

523
00:25:04,461 --> 00:25:06,046
<i>‪Round 1 will now begin.</i>

524
00:25:06,796 --> 00:25:09,257
<i>‪Please select your shape.</i>

525
00:25:09,341 --> 00:25:10,884
‪Now it's about who selects first.

526
00:25:10,967 --> 00:25:12,302
‪Let's read the room.

527
00:25:12,385 --> 00:25:13,929
‪-Can I ask you something?
‪-Yeah.

528
00:25:14,596 --> 00:25:16,598
‪You've been in prison the longest.

529
00:25:16,681 --> 00:25:18,683
‪Can you really trust the other two?

530
00:25:18,767 --> 00:25:19,601
‪No.

531
00:25:19,684 --> 00:25:20,560
‪-Not really, right?
‪-No.

532
00:25:20,644 --> 00:25:21,603
‪We should test them.

533
00:25:21,686 --> 00:25:26,733
‪Round 1 is basically a zeroing round,
‪like calibrating a gun.

534
00:25:26,816 --> 00:25:28,860
<i>‪I wanna see who shares real intel</i>

535
00:25:28,944 --> 00:25:31,238
<i>‪and who shares fake intel.</i>

536
00:25:31,321 --> 00:25:33,323
‪Can't trust Won-young, right?

537
00:25:34,282 --> 00:25:35,575
‪Or you can't trust both?

538
00:25:35,659 --> 00:25:36,785
‪Won-young.

539
00:25:36,868 --> 00:25:38,036
‪Right, it's Won-young who you can't trust.

540
00:25:38,119 --> 00:25:39,579
‪So let's test him.

541
00:25:39,663 --> 00:25:42,624
‪How about having one of us play solo?

542
00:25:42,707 --> 00:25:44,000
‪To stop information from leaking.

543
00:25:44,084 --> 00:25:45,669
‪We say one thing and do another.

544
00:25:47,170 --> 00:25:48,672
‪You can tell when someone's desperate.

545
00:25:48,755 --> 00:25:52,008
<i>‪John is an excellent player,</i>

546
00:25:52,092 --> 00:25:54,636
<i>‪but constantly ending up in prison</i>
<i>‪has knocked his confidence,</i>

547
00:25:54,719 --> 00:25:56,263
<i>‪so his desperation was noticeable.</i>

548
00:25:56,346 --> 00:26:00,016
‪Kyung-lyul also seemed
‪kind of desperate too.

549
00:26:00,100 --> 00:26:02,060
‪Being able to lie is a luxury.

550
00:26:02,143 --> 00:26:04,312
<i>‪Won-young can afford such luxuries.</i>

551
00:26:04,396 --> 00:26:05,939
‪-Okay?
‪-Okay.

552
00:26:06,022 --> 00:26:07,732
‪We're talking amongst ourselves

553
00:26:07,816 --> 00:26:09,859
‪because I think you two are trustworthy.

554
00:26:09,943 --> 00:26:12,988
‪-They've never reached out to us.
‪-Okay.

555
00:26:13,571 --> 00:26:14,823
‪I'm a prisoner too.

556
00:26:14,906 --> 00:26:16,324
‪-Let me join you.
‪-You sure?

557
00:26:16,408 --> 00:26:17,367
‪What?

558
00:26:17,450 --> 00:26:20,078
‪Then tell us
‪how much they're bidding on what.

559
00:26:26,626 --> 00:26:28,628
‪Is your plan to take down Dong-min?

560
00:26:29,254 --> 00:26:30,547
‪Yeah.

561
00:26:33,675 --> 00:26:36,511
‪The game makes it possible
‪to take him down.

562
00:26:36,594 --> 00:26:37,595
‪Right, it's doable.

563
00:26:37,679 --> 00:26:40,932
‪So I actually think we need to play this
‪like an actual survival show.

564
00:26:41,766 --> 00:26:44,019
‪-I'll share everything I know.
‪-Okay.

565
00:26:45,895 --> 00:26:49,482
‪Wouldn't it be smarter to have ORBIT
‪go for whatever Dong-min picks?

566
00:26:49,566 --> 00:26:52,152
‪That way, he can stay updated
‪and keep Dong-min in check.

567
00:26:52,235 --> 00:26:53,403
‪-Should we do that?
‪-Yeah.

568
00:26:53,486 --> 00:26:56,156
‪Then there's no risk for us either.

569
00:26:56,239 --> 00:26:57,657
‪Even if XITSUH tries to play us,

570
00:26:57,741 --> 00:26:59,701
‪-he can't hurt us.
‪-Not at all.

571
00:26:59,784 --> 00:27:02,704
‪Today, the only person I trust is ORBIT.

572
00:27:03,204 --> 00:27:04,581
‪First, let's do this.

573
00:27:05,832 --> 00:27:07,917
‪We need one two-won bid
‪and two one-won bids per shape.

574
00:27:08,001 --> 00:27:09,836
‪So they can't win it with just one won.

575
00:27:09,919 --> 00:27:10,879
‪Right.

576
00:27:10,962 --> 00:27:12,547
‪The one with the most Pieces
‪needs to keep them in--

577
00:27:12,630 --> 00:27:13,715
‪I can't hear you at all.

578
00:27:14,299 --> 00:27:15,216
‪Okay.

579
00:27:15,300 --> 00:27:17,761
‪-So you came to listen in.
‪-Scram, you dirty spy.

580
00:27:17,844 --> 00:27:21,139
‪-You came because you couldn't hear.
‪-My philosophy is happiness for all.

581
00:27:21,222 --> 00:27:22,265
‪-Okay, okay.
‪-You're happy, right?

582
00:27:22,349 --> 00:27:23,183
‪I'm not.

583
00:27:23,266 --> 00:27:24,893
‪-How come?
‪-You're targeting me.

584
00:27:24,976 --> 00:27:26,144
‪-No, Dong-min.
‪-So how could I be?

585
00:27:26,227 --> 00:27:28,521
‪You have a flawed philosophy.

586
00:27:29,147 --> 00:27:32,150
‪-You help one to make another miserable.
‪-No, not at all.

587
00:27:32,233 --> 00:27:34,402
‪If you wanna make the majority happy,

588
00:27:34,486 --> 00:27:36,112
‪just stay quietly out of the way.

589
00:27:36,654 --> 00:27:38,448
‪Got that?

590
00:27:38,531 --> 00:27:41,368
‪Last night, XITSUH suggested
‪that it might be time

591
00:27:41,451 --> 00:27:43,661
‪-Right, to make a move.
‪-to strike the big guy.

592
00:27:43,745 --> 00:27:46,748
‪That's what he said to me,
‪and I think he meant it.

593
00:27:46,831 --> 00:27:49,125
‪Dong-jae said something similar too.

594
00:27:49,209 --> 00:27:51,378
‪I told him
‪that if he could really trust me

595
00:27:51,461 --> 00:27:53,588
‪and betray Dong-min
‪to make me first place,

596
00:27:53,671 --> 00:27:58,426
‪I'd use the salvation token
‪or the alliance token to save him.

597
00:27:58,510 --> 00:28:00,762
‪I offered,
‪but he probably won't go for it.

598
00:28:00,845 --> 00:28:01,971
‪Right.

599
00:28:02,680 --> 00:28:05,100
‪Things haven't been easy
‪between Kyung-lyul and me,

600
00:28:05,183 --> 00:28:06,810
‪so if I get the chance to use the token,

601
00:28:06,893 --> 00:28:08,895
‪-I think it's right that I use it on you.
‪-Right.

602
00:28:08,978 --> 00:28:10,397
‪-I'll abandon Dong-jae.
‪-Okay.

603
00:28:14,484 --> 00:28:15,318
‪That's…

604
00:28:15,944 --> 00:28:17,487
‪-That's up to you.
‪-Yeah, my choice.

605
00:28:17,570 --> 00:28:19,781
‪You do what you need to do.

606
00:28:20,281 --> 00:28:23,410
‪I'll make a bid alone for whichever shape
‪their highest Piece holder goes for.

607
00:28:23,993 --> 00:28:25,995
‪Shouldn't we be careful
‪about whatever ORBIT chooses?

608
00:28:26,079 --> 00:28:28,581
‪A radical person like him can drop a bomb.

609
00:28:28,665 --> 00:28:31,334
‪I'll go talk to him about that.

610
00:28:32,502 --> 00:28:33,962
‪-ORBIT.
‪-Yes?

611
00:28:34,587 --> 00:28:37,090
‪-It's great that you're playing with us.
‪-Okay.

612
00:28:37,173 --> 00:28:38,174
‪That's fun and all.

613
00:28:38,258 --> 00:28:42,262
‪But there's one thing
‪I really hope you won't do.

614
00:28:42,345 --> 00:28:44,514
‪-We need a strategy too.
‪-Of course.

615
00:28:44,597 --> 00:28:47,434
‪So don't pull out all the stops
‪to box me out, okay?

616
00:28:47,517 --> 00:28:48,935
‪You know how I roll.

617
00:28:49,018 --> 00:28:50,937
‪I always pull out all the stops.

618
00:28:51,521 --> 00:28:52,647
‪I'll be using my Piece too.

619
00:28:52,731 --> 00:28:54,107
‪Do you have a plan?

620
00:28:54,607 --> 00:28:56,484
‪It'll be all out in the open anyway.

621
00:28:56,568 --> 00:28:57,986
‪-Right.
‪-We can't really…

622
00:28:58,069 --> 00:28:59,863
‪-What I meant was…
‪-We'll probably split up too.

623
00:28:59,946 --> 00:29:00,989
‪I was actually asking

624
00:29:01,573 --> 00:29:03,742
‪if you're planning to stick with Dong-min.

625
00:29:04,868 --> 00:29:06,453
‪I'm sticking with him for now.

626
00:29:06,536 --> 00:29:07,662
‪-Yeah?
‪-Yeah.

627
00:29:07,746 --> 00:29:09,831
‪At least for now. What are you thinking?

628
00:29:10,415 --> 00:29:14,377
‪I'm sure everyone wants to see Dong-min
‪make it to the finals,

629
00:29:14,961 --> 00:29:16,421
‪but I came to win.

630
00:29:16,504 --> 00:29:19,215
‪If we're gonna strike,
‪now might be the moment.

631
00:29:20,049 --> 00:29:20,884
‪That's where I'm at.

632
00:29:21,593 --> 00:29:22,552
‪I see.

633
00:29:22,635 --> 00:29:23,845
‪Let me think about it.

634
00:29:23,928 --> 00:29:25,638
‪-Sorry?
‪-Let me think about it.

635
00:29:25,722 --> 00:29:28,767
‪Of course, Dong-min is the biggest threat.

636
00:29:28,850 --> 00:29:30,435
‪So I'm hoping

637
00:29:30,518 --> 00:29:32,187
‪he gets eliminated today.

638
00:29:32,270 --> 00:29:34,272
‪Either way, my goal is to find a balance--

639
00:29:34,355 --> 00:29:36,024
‪They brought the wrong guy back.

640
00:29:36,608 --> 00:29:39,611
‪Why would they bring that punk,
‪out of all people?

641
00:29:39,694 --> 00:29:42,322
‪Seriously? Damn it.

642
00:29:42,405 --> 00:29:43,448
‪Oh dear.

643
00:29:44,532 --> 00:29:45,784
‪-Talk didn't go well?
‪-What?

644
00:29:45,867 --> 00:29:46,701
‪Is he dropping a bomb?

645
00:29:46,785 --> 00:29:48,703
‪Who knows? He's impossible.

646
00:29:48,787 --> 00:29:51,873
‪-So many impossible people here.
‪-One minute until the shape selection.

647
00:29:51,956 --> 00:29:52,957
‪-We have one minute left.
‪-Okay.

648
00:29:53,041 --> 00:29:55,877
‪ORBIT, one minute left!

649
00:29:56,753 --> 00:29:58,004
‪Let's try to cover it up.

650
00:29:58,838 --> 00:29:59,839
‪I wanna go here.

651
00:30:00,965 --> 00:30:02,008
‪Just go for it?

652
00:30:02,592 --> 00:30:03,426
‪Do it.

653
00:30:04,677 --> 00:30:06,763
‪So what should we do?
‪We need to put it in fast.

654
00:30:06,846 --> 00:30:11,935
‪You need to decide who in your group
‪is gonna take it in the end.

655
00:30:12,018 --> 00:30:13,186
‪Someone needs to bid one won,

656
00:30:13,269 --> 00:30:16,356
‪and the other needs to bid high to win it.

657
00:30:16,439 --> 00:30:18,024
‪I can definitely win this one.

658
00:30:18,107 --> 00:30:19,609
‪-You can?
‪-Yeah, I can.

659
00:30:19,692 --> 00:30:21,277
‪Then I'll support you. What do you want?

660
00:30:21,361 --> 00:30:22,487
‪Right, even just one's fine.

661
00:30:22,570 --> 00:30:23,488
‪In that case…

662
00:30:23,571 --> 00:30:24,906
‪I'll go for the circle.

663
00:30:24,989 --> 00:30:27,575
‪-Then we'll bid on the triangle.
‪-Okay.

664
00:30:28,076 --> 00:30:29,410
‪Go for it, Dong-min.

665
00:30:29,494 --> 00:30:30,495
‪You go ahead.

666
00:30:30,995 --> 00:30:32,705
‪I need to stay a bit hidden.

667
00:30:32,789 --> 00:30:33,665
‪No, you can't.

668
00:30:33,748 --> 00:30:34,916
‪You go first.

669
00:30:34,999 --> 00:30:35,834
‪I refuse to go first.

670
00:30:35,917 --> 00:30:37,710
‪If you've come to mess things up,

671
00:30:37,794 --> 00:30:40,380
‪-this is the least you can do.
‪-Triangle.

672
00:30:40,463 --> 00:30:42,131
‪-Triangle.
‪-Everyone done?

673
00:30:42,215 --> 00:30:44,300
‪You're all watching anyway.

674
00:30:44,384 --> 00:30:46,302
‪-Could I get some space?
‪-Sure.

675
00:30:46,386 --> 00:30:49,347
‪-I already made up my mind.
‪-I'll vote openly and proudly.

676
00:30:49,430 --> 00:30:50,348
‪Okay.

677
00:30:50,431 --> 00:30:52,433
‪-Triangle is popular. Two bidders already.
‪-XITSUH first.

678
00:30:52,517 --> 00:30:54,060
‪Go ahead with the exit poll.

679
00:30:55,186 --> 00:30:57,689
‪-It'll get revealed anyway.
‪-Yeah, no point in covering.

680
00:30:57,772 --> 00:30:58,773
‪-Okay.
‪-Okay.

681
00:30:58,857 --> 00:31:01,025
‪-The triangle is popular.
‪-Bid on whatever Dong-min bids on.

682
00:31:02,318 --> 00:31:03,778
‪Dong-min hasn't selected yet, right?

683
00:31:03,862 --> 00:31:05,572
‪Go ahead and place yours first.

684
00:31:05,655 --> 00:31:07,407
‪-Do it already!
‪-Should we do it together?

685
00:31:07,490 --> 00:31:09,284
‪-No.
‪-Just give me yours.

686
00:31:09,367 --> 00:31:11,327
‪The worst sportsmanship ever.

687
00:31:12,036 --> 00:31:14,080
‪-Seriously, that punk.
‪-How do you define sportsmanship?

688
00:31:14,163 --> 00:31:16,249
‪-He refused to budge yesterday too.
‪-We already went first.

689
00:31:16,332 --> 00:31:18,376
‪-How do you define sportsmanship?
‪-Who went already?

690
00:31:18,459 --> 00:31:19,586
‪-We all did.
‪-Who?

691
00:31:19,669 --> 00:31:21,796
‪-Everyone except ORBIT.
‪-What did you choose?

692
00:31:21,880 --> 00:31:23,715
‪I went for the square.

693
00:31:23,798 --> 00:31:24,757
‪I went for the moon.

694
00:31:25,675 --> 00:31:27,051
‪-Moon?
‪-I went for the sun.

695
00:31:27,135 --> 00:31:29,012
‪I'll go after ORBIT makes his selection.

696
00:31:29,095 --> 00:31:31,681
‪You have five Pieces.

697
00:31:31,764 --> 00:31:33,641
‪You can at least do this much for us.

698
00:31:33,725 --> 00:31:37,729
‪You expect me to follow your insane logic
‪just for an even playing field?

699
00:31:37,812 --> 00:31:39,606
‪-What do we do?
‪-This is nonsense.

700
00:31:39,689 --> 00:31:41,149
‪-This is…
‪-Then how about this?

701
00:31:41,232 --> 00:31:43,735
‪-You just--
‪-Since there are seven rounds,

702
00:31:43,818 --> 00:31:45,862
‪I'll go first for four of those rounds.

703
00:31:45,945 --> 00:31:47,530
‪You go first for three of them.

704
00:31:47,614 --> 00:31:50,241
‪If you can't even agree to that,
‪I'll be at too much of a disadvantage.

705
00:31:50,325 --> 00:31:51,409
‪-Okay, fine.
‪-Let's be fair about it.

706
00:31:51,492 --> 00:31:53,244
‪-Then I'll go first in Round 1.
‪-Okay.

707
00:31:55,371 --> 00:31:57,582
‪I've selected the triangle.

708
00:32:00,960 --> 00:32:03,296
<i>‪Shape selection is now closed.</i>

709
00:32:03,379 --> 00:32:06,883
<i>‪Here are the shapes</i>
<i>‪each </i><i>‪player </i><i>‪has </i><i>‪selected.</i>

710
00:32:06,966 --> 00:32:07,884
‪How annoying.

711
00:32:07,967 --> 00:32:09,302
‪So that's how it turned out.

712
00:32:10,178 --> 00:32:12,347
‪Now the star
‪will definitely remain a secret.

713
00:32:12,430 --> 00:32:14,682
‪He'll just spend
‪a ton of Pieces and take it.

714
00:32:14,766 --> 00:32:16,059
‪We're both going for the triangle.

715
00:32:16,142 --> 00:32:17,644
‪-Oh, we are.
‪-Bid low.

716
00:32:17,727 --> 00:32:20,063
‪We have to keep these guys in check,
‪so Kyung-lyul has to bid high,

717
00:32:20,146 --> 00:32:22,273
‪and I'll try to find out
‪how much Dong-min's bidding on it.

718
00:32:22,357 --> 00:32:24,567
<i>‪Bidding will now begin.</i>

719
00:32:24,651 --> 00:32:28,446
<i>‪You have 20 minutes to place your bids.</i>

720
00:32:28,529 --> 00:32:31,074
‪Should the competing bidders
‪talk amongst themselves?

721
00:32:31,157 --> 00:32:33,076
‪Is there any need for that?

722
00:32:33,159 --> 00:32:34,285
‪I don't get that either.

723
00:32:34,369 --> 00:32:35,662
‪We don't have to.

724
00:32:36,454 --> 00:32:38,331
‪I'd rather not.

725
00:32:38,414 --> 00:32:39,332
‪-Really?
‪-Yeah.

726
00:32:39,415 --> 00:32:42,126
‪-I don't think we should.
‪-Why advise him against a good offer?

727
00:32:42,210 --> 00:32:45,505
‪-Aren't you on their side?
‪-Because you're too much of a strategist.

728
00:32:45,588 --> 00:32:48,383
‪-He'll figure me out if I say anything.
‪-Suit yourself, then.

729
00:32:48,466 --> 00:32:50,343
‪Can the prison team gather for a second?

730
00:32:50,426 --> 00:32:52,136
‪I almost followed them.

731
00:32:52,220 --> 00:32:54,764
‪Let's gather by ourselves and talk.

732
00:32:54,847 --> 00:32:57,350
‪I need to go upstairs now.
‪Let's talk later.

733
00:32:57,433 --> 00:32:59,477
‪Just tell me which of us it's gonna be.

734
00:32:59,560 --> 00:33:01,604
‪I can't right now.
‪I have to see what happens.

735
00:33:01,688 --> 00:33:02,647
‪Just wait.

736
00:33:07,610 --> 00:33:09,737
‪Won-young's not here yet.

737
00:33:09,821 --> 00:33:11,739
‪I do think we need to test him.

738
00:33:11,823 --> 00:33:12,824
‪We need to see first.

739
00:33:12,907 --> 00:33:16,869
‪Either way, my loyalty
‪isn't to an individual but a group.

740
00:33:16,953 --> 00:33:19,789
‪-This group needs to secure the advantage.
‪-That's reassuring.

741
00:33:19,872 --> 00:33:22,667
‪It'll be an individual game
‪in the end anyway.

742
00:33:22,750 --> 00:33:24,377
‪You're one-on-one. What'd you two decide?

743
00:33:24,460 --> 00:33:25,878
‪What did you and Dong-jae talk about?

744
00:33:26,421 --> 00:33:29,132
‪Playing rock-paper-scissors
‪to decide who wins which rounds.

745
00:33:29,215 --> 00:33:31,050
‪Don't agree to that.

746
00:33:31,134 --> 00:33:32,844
‪Let's just each take a shape.

747
00:33:33,428 --> 00:33:34,345
‪That's the way to go.

748
00:33:34,429 --> 00:33:36,639
‪I'll take the triangle.

749
00:33:37,473 --> 00:33:42,186
‪I feel like they won't expect me
‪to really go for it.

750
00:33:42,270 --> 00:33:44,147
‪-I'll go all out this time.
‪-All out?

751
00:33:44,230 --> 00:33:45,481
‪Yeah, just this once.

752
00:33:45,565 --> 00:33:49,402
‪But I'd rather you go all out
‪when you're against Dong-min.

753
00:33:49,485 --> 00:33:53,322
‪No, since there are four of us right now,
‪this is clearly a throwaway round.

754
00:33:53,406 --> 00:33:56,159
‪But we wanna protect your money.

755
00:33:56,826 --> 00:33:59,620
‪-Bid one when you're not against Dong-min.
‪-So don't waste my money.

756
00:33:59,704 --> 00:34:01,873
‪This is so damn annoying.

757
00:34:02,623 --> 00:34:04,917
‪ORBIT alone has completely
‪messed things up.

758
00:34:05,001 --> 00:34:08,129
‪Damn it, I shouldn't have
‪gone for the star this time.

759
00:34:08,212 --> 00:34:10,381
‪"Don't spend money
‪if you're not up against Dong-min."

760
00:34:10,465 --> 00:34:15,470
‪"Only spend it when you're trying to
‪stop him from winning the shape."

761
00:34:15,553 --> 00:34:17,138
<i>‪That's their strategy.</i>

762
00:34:17,221 --> 00:34:18,222
‪Dong-min, we should…

763
00:34:18,306 --> 00:34:20,058
‪-Yeah, go ahead.
‪-While you take a breather,

764
00:34:20,141 --> 00:34:21,601
‪-we need to figure this out.
‪-Right.

765
00:34:21,684 --> 00:34:24,562
‪Four people are going for the triangle,

766
00:34:24,645 --> 00:34:26,105
‪and we can't just give that up.

767
00:34:26,189 --> 00:34:27,440
‪-Sorry.
‪-It's okay.

768
00:34:27,523 --> 00:34:28,733
‪-Work on it.
‪-Try to calm down.

769
00:34:28,816 --> 00:34:30,985
‪-I'm gonna step out to think about it.
‪-Sure.

770
00:34:37,658 --> 00:34:39,077
‪So what's the plan?

771
00:34:39,160 --> 00:34:42,246
‪-I'm thinking about bidding seven.
‪-For him, it's a one-on-one mind game.

772
00:34:42,330 --> 00:34:43,956
‪Seven? That's a bit iffy.

773
00:34:44,040 --> 00:34:45,875
‪How much do you think it'll take to win?

774
00:34:45,958 --> 00:34:47,919
‪Maybe a bit more, like eight?

775
00:34:48,002 --> 00:34:49,962
‪No, if I'm going for it,
‪I should go big, like 13.

776
00:34:50,046 --> 00:34:50,922
‪How's 15?

777
00:34:51,005 --> 00:34:52,757
‪-That's too much.
‪-Sixteen.

778
00:34:52,840 --> 00:34:55,301
‪-Seriously?
‪-It's over for me if I lose that.

779
00:34:55,384 --> 00:34:57,345
‪If he wins, he gets two stars.

780
00:34:57,428 --> 00:34:58,888
‪But if I lose, I'll be eliminated.

781
00:34:58,971 --> 00:35:00,848
‪Can you still win
‪a circle or triangle bid after this?

782
00:35:01,516 --> 00:35:02,892
‪It's the same for us.

783
00:35:04,310 --> 00:35:06,938
‪If both Kyung-lyul and I
‪don't win the star…

784
00:35:08,898 --> 00:35:10,942
‪Who's gonna win the triangle bid
‪this round?

785
00:35:11,025 --> 00:35:14,362
‪Yurisa agreed to lay the groundwork first,
‪then I'll back her up next.

786
00:35:14,445 --> 00:35:17,281
‪I don't think ORBIT
‪will spend too much at the start.

787
00:35:17,365 --> 00:35:19,492
‪-You think so?
‪-I think he's only focused on Dong-min.

788
00:35:19,575 --> 00:35:22,537
‪So it comes down to how much John spends.

789
00:35:25,748 --> 00:35:27,416
‪-That looks good.
‪-Hello.

790
00:35:28,417 --> 00:35:31,045
‪-How much is Dong-min spending?
‪-He's pretty riled up right now.

791
00:35:31,129 --> 00:35:33,297
‪-It's fine. I'm close to Dong-min.
‪-Is he alone right now?

792
00:35:33,381 --> 00:35:35,216
‪Yeah, he is.

793
00:35:35,299 --> 00:35:37,218
‪You get the overall situation, right?

794
00:35:37,301 --> 00:35:38,970
‪-What are you gonna do?
‪-Well…

795
00:35:39,053 --> 00:35:40,638
‪I'm here to talk to John.

796
00:35:40,721 --> 00:35:44,058
‪Bid two won. John will do the same.
‪You guys can win two each.

797
00:35:44,142 --> 00:35:45,601
‪We don't need that many triangles anyway.

798
00:35:45,685 --> 00:35:47,562
‪-How about three?
‪-Three? Okay.

799
00:35:47,645 --> 00:35:51,065
‪It'll look like we suddenly
‪landed on three after playing mind games.

800
00:35:51,149 --> 00:35:52,733
‪Do you wanna negotiate the circle bid?

801
00:35:52,817 --> 00:35:53,860
‪Would you be willing?

802
00:35:53,943 --> 00:35:56,571
‪I trust you,
‪but I'm worried you don't trust me.

803
00:35:56,654 --> 00:35:59,699
‪It's pointless
‪to bleed each other out this time.

804
00:35:59,782 --> 00:36:02,201
‪We'll have to bid
‪on the circle again, right?

805
00:36:02,285 --> 00:36:03,744
‪If we can agree to bid one each,

806
00:36:03,828 --> 00:36:05,746
‪-We need four total.
‪-I'm willing.

807
00:36:07,832 --> 00:36:08,749
‪Hello.

808
00:36:09,333 --> 00:36:10,710
‪Here is your coin pouch.

809
00:36:10,793 --> 00:36:12,378
‪Please submit your coins.

810
00:36:19,177 --> 00:36:20,428
‪I really hope he bid one.

811
00:36:21,304 --> 00:36:23,347
‪He bid one, right?

812
00:36:23,431 --> 00:36:25,308
‪-I cannot disclose that.
‪-Right.

813
00:36:25,391 --> 00:36:27,268
‪-I'll bid one won.
‪-Sure.

814
00:36:28,936 --> 00:36:30,146
‪You have bid one won.

815
00:36:30,229 --> 00:36:33,733
‪-Kyung-lyul has to win two stars.
‪-I'm gonna bid three won, then.

816
00:36:33,816 --> 00:36:36,319
‪-Go ahead.
‪-Kyung-lyul, you have to win this bid.

817
00:36:36,402 --> 00:36:39,614
‪I <i>‪have to </i>‪win? There's no need to say that
‪in front of XITSUH.

818
00:36:42,241 --> 00:36:43,659
‪You have to win, okay?

819
00:36:43,743 --> 00:36:45,328
‪IT'S A LIE

820
00:36:45,411 --> 00:36:46,787
‪Then how many should I bid?

821
00:36:46,871 --> 00:36:49,832
‪Everything I say to you from now on
‪will mean the exact opposite.

822
00:36:50,750 --> 00:36:53,377
‪Bid 18 for now.

823
00:36:53,461 --> 00:36:55,671
‪-Because you have to…
‪-Are you trying to play mind games?

824
00:36:55,755 --> 00:36:57,340
‪She's throwing this one out,

825
00:36:57,423 --> 00:36:58,799
‪-so she'll probably bid one.
‪-I've talked to XITSUH,

826
00:36:59,383 --> 00:37:00,718
‪so we can both win.

827
00:37:01,302 --> 00:37:02,720
‪-So, for now…
‪-I just wanna see first.

828
00:37:02,803 --> 00:37:04,138
‪-Eighteen, right?
‪-Yeah.

829
00:37:04,222 --> 00:37:06,682
‪We're set.

830
00:37:06,766 --> 00:37:08,768
‪Kyung-lyul has to win this bid.

831
00:37:08,851 --> 00:37:09,977
‪-He'll be set with two stars.
‪-Right.

832
00:37:10,061 --> 00:37:12,146
‪Even if they go big, I think it'll be 15.

833
00:37:12,230 --> 00:37:14,148
‪-So we need to bid 16 to win.
‪-Okay.

834
00:37:17,235 --> 00:37:18,945
‪Everything I say is the opposite, got it?

835
00:37:19,028 --> 00:37:21,447
‪How much am I supposed to lose?
‪I mean, how much do I bid?

836
00:37:21,530 --> 00:37:22,907
‪-Just bid three.
‪-Three.

837
00:37:23,407 --> 00:37:27,828
‪If Dong-min loses and you win it,

838
00:37:27,912 --> 00:37:30,706
‪-That'd be amazing.
‪-that'd mean Won-young's on our side.

839
00:37:30,790 --> 00:37:32,458
‪But if Dong-min wins,

840
00:37:32,541 --> 00:37:35,169
‪there's a good chance
‪Won-young's on their side.

841
00:37:35,253 --> 00:37:36,587
‪I'd like to exchange my Pieces.

842
00:37:36,671 --> 00:37:38,130
‪-How many?
‪-Two.

843
00:37:38,214 --> 00:37:39,548
‪Please submit two Pieces.

844
00:37:39,632 --> 00:37:41,133
‪How do I finish all this in one minute?

845
00:37:41,217 --> 00:37:43,636
‪-Here's two won.
‪-Thank you.

846
00:37:43,719 --> 00:37:45,137
‪I'll bid one won.

847
00:37:47,932 --> 00:37:49,767
‪You have bid one three-won coin.

848
00:37:49,850 --> 00:37:51,185
‪Three won.

849
00:37:53,646 --> 00:37:55,731
‪Kyung-lyul, you're not gonna talk, right?

850
00:37:56,315 --> 00:37:57,233
‪-No.
‪-What?

851
00:37:57,316 --> 00:37:59,986
‪-I'll be at a disadvantage.
‪-You can talk science with me.

852
00:38:00,069 --> 00:38:02,321
‪I told you I don't wanna talk to you.

853
00:38:02,405 --> 00:38:03,322
‪Do I put it in?

854
00:38:06,117 --> 00:38:07,994
‪You have bid one three-won coin.

855
00:38:12,456 --> 00:38:14,625
‪DEALER ROOM

856
00:38:15,876 --> 00:38:17,586
<i>‪Bidding is now complete.</i>

857
00:38:18,337 --> 00:38:21,465
<i>‪Here is the winning bid for each shape.</i>

858
00:38:21,549 --> 00:38:22,883
‪-What the?
‪-Oh, shit.

859
00:38:22,967 --> 00:38:23,968
‪△: 3 WON, ◯: 1 WON, ☆: SECRET

860
00:38:24,051 --> 00:38:25,970
‪"Secret" must mean…

861
00:38:26,762 --> 00:38:29,098
‪So the winning bid for the star
‪was more than three won.

862
00:38:30,141 --> 00:38:31,851
‪That means he bid four or more.

863
00:38:31,934 --> 00:38:33,936
‪The fact that there's a secret on the star

864
00:38:34,020 --> 00:38:38,065
‪means Dong-min bid more than I did,
‪so four won or more.

865
00:38:38,149 --> 00:38:41,402
‪So he's definitely won
‪both stars right now.

866
