1083
00:47:59,918 --> 00:48:02,796
‪-You have bid one two-won coin.
‪-Yes.

1084
00:48:03,839 --> 00:48:05,132
‪Please submit your coins.

1085
00:48:08,552 --> 00:48:10,262
<i>‪Bidding is now complete.</i>

1086
00:48:10,804 --> 00:48:14,016
<i>‪Here is the winning bid for each shape.</i>

1087
00:48:14,099 --> 00:48:15,726
‪△: SECRET, ◯: 3 WON, ☆: 1 WON

1088
00:48:15,809 --> 00:48:17,644
‪Kyung-lyul must've bid three won.

1089
00:48:17,728 --> 00:48:19,229
‪-You bid one won?
‪-I bid two.

1090
00:48:19,313 --> 00:48:20,480
‪-You bid two won?
‪-Yeah.

1091
00:48:20,564 --> 00:48:22,357
‪Wait, then who bid three won?

1092
00:48:22,441 --> 00:48:23,900
‪Why did you bid three won?

1093
00:48:23,984 --> 00:48:25,527
‪-I bid two.
‪-What?

1094
00:48:25,611 --> 00:48:27,904
‪-He lied. I knew you would.
‪-No, wait.

1095
00:48:28,405 --> 00:48:30,949
‪-Don't lie, seriously.
‪-Are you sure you bid two won?

1096
00:48:31,033 --> 00:48:32,492
‪-I'm sure.
‪-Maybe you mixed up the coins.

1097
00:48:32,576 --> 00:48:33,493
‪Then you two bid three won.

1098
00:48:33,577 --> 00:48:35,329
‪-I swear I didn't.
‪-I didn't.

1099
00:48:35,412 --> 00:48:36,496
‪Then both of you bid one won?

1100
00:48:36,580 --> 00:48:38,081
‪-Yeah.
‪-I swear I did.

1101
00:48:38,165 --> 00:48:41,084
‪If she bid two won, and you two bid one,
‪then why is the winning bid three?

1102
00:48:41,168 --> 00:48:42,919
‪-I don't get it.
‪-Why would I bid three?

1103
00:48:43,003 --> 00:48:44,046
‪I swear it wasn't me.

1104
00:48:44,129 --> 00:48:45,922
‪-Me neither.
‪-Am I making sense?

1105
00:48:46,506 --> 00:48:48,300
‪I don't understand what happened.

1106
00:48:48,383 --> 00:48:50,093
‪-What happened?
‪-I'm not insane. Why would I?

1107
00:48:50,177 --> 00:48:51,762
‪I could've bid four or five.

1108
00:48:51,845 --> 00:48:52,971
‪What happened?

1109
00:48:53,764 --> 00:48:55,849
‪Come to think of it,
‪it feels like a waste to bid just one won.

1110
00:48:57,392 --> 00:48:58,435
‪But a promise is a promise.

1111
00:49:00,812 --> 00:49:02,814
‪-You have bid one one-won coin.
‪-Yes.

1112
00:49:06,818 --> 00:49:08,195
‪This is the three-won coin, right?

1113
00:49:09,905 --> 00:49:12,783
‪You have bid one three-won coin.

1114
00:49:12,866 --> 00:49:14,326
‪It's Kyung-lyul.

1115
00:49:14,409 --> 00:49:15,911
‪No, it wasn't me.

1116
00:49:15,994 --> 00:49:17,537
‪I swear I bid one won.

1117
00:49:18,038 --> 00:49:19,748
‪He's not the type to put on an act.

1118
00:49:20,624 --> 00:49:22,417
‪Don't tell me you suspect me.

1119
00:49:22,501 --> 00:49:24,002
‪You're really suspicious right now.

1120
00:49:24,086 --> 00:49:26,546
‪If I had been planning to bid three,
‪would I have gone in first?

1121
00:49:27,756 --> 00:49:28,799
‪How'd it go?

1122
00:49:29,758 --> 00:49:33,136
‪I lied to them and won all three circles.

1123
00:49:33,804 --> 00:49:36,098
‪How much was the winning bid?

1124
00:49:36,181 --> 00:49:37,432
‪Three won.

1125
00:49:37,516 --> 00:49:39,351
‪Three? And did you get everything?

1126
00:49:39,434 --> 00:49:42,312
‪Yurisa didn't, so Kyung-lyul swept it.

1127
00:49:42,396 --> 00:49:45,190
‪-But he kept saying it wasn't him.
‪-Why'd you team up with Kyung-lyul?

1128
00:49:45,273 --> 00:49:46,900
‪I didn't team up.

1129
00:49:46,983 --> 00:49:48,777
‪I just told him what I was bidding,
‪and they worked it out.

1130
00:49:48,860 --> 00:49:50,654
‪Then did you talk to Kyung-lyul?

1131
00:49:50,737 --> 00:49:54,032
‪-You need to talk to the right people.
‪-What did you tell him?

1132
00:49:54,116 --> 00:49:56,243
‪You can't talk to someone
‪who's gone off the rails.

1133
00:49:56,326 --> 00:49:58,954
‪Seriously.
‪Why didn't you come to me first?

1134
00:49:59,955 --> 00:50:01,790
<i>‪Round 3 will now begin.</i>

1135
00:50:02,624 --> 00:50:05,377
<i>‪Please select your shape.</i>

1136
00:50:05,460 --> 00:50:06,503
‪I lost.

1137
00:50:06,586 --> 00:50:08,046
‪They must've won it.

1138
00:50:08,130 --> 00:50:09,381
‪-Won-young?
‪-Yeah.

1139
00:50:09,464 --> 00:50:11,091
‪Why did Won-young jump in on this?

1140
00:50:11,174 --> 00:50:13,135
‪He won a circle earlier.

1141
00:50:13,218 --> 00:50:14,720
‪-In Round 1.
‪-Right.

1142
00:50:14,803 --> 00:50:17,431
‪Triangles could put him ahead,

1143
00:50:17,514 --> 00:50:20,600
‪so he probably bid a lot this time.

1144
00:50:21,184 --> 00:50:22,728
‪Did I overdo it?

1145
00:50:22,811 --> 00:50:26,273
‪Round 2 was important because there were
‪three people bidding on the triangle.

1146
00:50:26,356 --> 00:50:29,067
<i>‪So I just figured</i>
<i>‪that Dong-min would bid about ten won,</i>

1147
00:50:29,151 --> 00:50:33,363
<i>‪which is roughly 1.5 times</i>
<i>‪the average of 7.</i>

1148
00:50:33,447 --> 00:50:36,241
‪I was considering 12 or 13.

1149
00:50:36,324 --> 00:50:38,994
<i>‪Then I even pushed it</i>
<i>‪to the worst-case scenario,</i>

1150
00:50:39,077 --> 00:50:40,787
<i>‪and ended up with an excessive bid of 14.</i>

1151
00:50:40,871 --> 00:50:42,497
‪I'm sure you won it.

1152
00:50:42,581 --> 00:50:44,374
‪You're going last this round, right?

1153
00:50:44,458 --> 00:50:45,751
‪I have to select first.

1154
00:50:45,834 --> 00:50:48,503
‪-Can you go for the star with me?
‪-Star?

1155
00:50:48,587 --> 00:50:50,338
‪Dong-min won't bid on the star anyway.

1156
00:50:50,422 --> 00:50:52,591
‪Since he won't be bidding on it,

1157
00:50:53,300 --> 00:50:55,969
‪it doesn't make sense for me to go for it.

1158
00:50:56,052 --> 00:50:58,889
‪Think about it. Selecting the star
‪when I know Dong-min won't go for it

1159
00:50:58,972 --> 00:50:59,806
‪will be pointless.

1160
00:50:59,890 --> 00:51:03,059
‪I'll go for the circle or the triangle,
‪whichever attracts more of their team.

1161
00:51:03,143 --> 00:51:05,270
‪-Okay.
‪-I'll be sticking to that rule.

1162
00:51:06,188 --> 00:51:08,190
‪-Do you have a way out right now?
‪-I'm in trouble.

1163
00:51:08,273 --> 00:51:09,775
‪-Anything we can help with?
‪-No.

1164
00:51:09,858 --> 00:51:11,902
‪I'm kind of at a dead end.

1165
00:51:17,991 --> 00:51:19,075
‪I'll go first.

1166
00:51:24,623 --> 00:51:25,707
‪Whatever.

1167
00:51:29,544 --> 00:51:30,796
‪We need to take out Won-young.

1168
00:51:30,879 --> 00:51:34,299
<i>‪If Won-young locked down</i>
<i>‪3 triangles in Round 2,</i>

1169
00:51:34,382 --> 00:51:36,927
‪then two stars would leave him
‪in a very advantageous position.

1170
00:51:37,010 --> 00:51:38,637
‪He'd just need more circles.

1171
00:51:42,098 --> 00:51:43,350
‪Who's gonna bid on the circle?

1172
00:51:43,433 --> 00:51:44,601
‪Can I go for it?

1173
00:51:44,684 --> 00:51:46,102
‪Then let's bid on it together.

1174
00:51:46,186 --> 00:51:47,229
‪-Together?
‪-Yeah.

1175
00:51:47,312 --> 00:51:48,980
‪You go for the triangle.

1176
00:51:49,064 --> 00:51:50,065
‪I'll win this bid.

1177
00:51:50,148 --> 00:51:51,608
‪-Okay.
‪-I'll win it somehow.

1178
00:51:52,234 --> 00:51:53,610
‪I wanna see what they're choosing.

1179
00:51:53,693 --> 00:51:54,778
‪What are you choosing?

1180
00:51:59,950 --> 00:52:02,077
‪Okay, in that case…

1181
00:52:02,828 --> 00:52:07,457
‪At the end of the day,
‪I have to block Dong-min.

1182
00:52:16,383 --> 00:52:18,552
<i>‪Shape selection is now closed.</i>

1183
00:52:18,635 --> 00:52:21,721
<i>‪Here are the shapes</i>
<i>‪each </i><i>‪player </i><i>‪has </i><i>‪selected.</i>

1184
00:52:23,306 --> 00:52:24,349
‪Everyone's gathered there.

1185
00:52:24,432 --> 00:52:25,934
‪It's a circle fight.

1186
00:52:26,017 --> 00:52:28,937
‪Let's say I stab you in the back
‪and take two.

1187
00:52:29,020 --> 00:52:31,106
‪I'll have to come back at some point
‪to win another triangle.

1188
00:52:31,189 --> 00:52:33,692
‪I can guarantee you
‪that I'm gonna bid one won.

1189
00:52:33,775 --> 00:52:35,277
‪I'm gonna bid one won.

1190
00:52:35,360 --> 00:52:37,654
‪I can go first.
‪That'll give you more reason to trust me.

1191
00:52:37,737 --> 00:52:39,531
‪-That's true.
‪-Okay.

1192
00:52:39,614 --> 00:52:41,825
‪-I'm trusting you.
‪-I'd never stab you in the back.

1193
00:52:42,409 --> 00:52:43,702
‪Please submit your coins.

1194
00:52:45,078 --> 00:52:46,246
‪One.

1195
00:52:46,329 --> 00:52:48,623
‪You have bid one one-won coin.

1196
00:52:50,208 --> 00:52:51,501
‪I'll bid seven won.

1197
00:52:52,085 --> 00:52:56,172
‪You have bid one five-won coin
‪and one two-won coin, totaling seven won.

1198
00:52:56,256 --> 00:52:59,009
‪-Well, I'm…
‪-You managed to secure a few safely.

1199
00:52:59,092 --> 00:53:02,971
‪I'm only sharing this because
‪I trust you'll protect the underdogs.

1200
00:53:03,054 --> 00:53:04,764
‪-Please keep this confidential.
‪-Of course.

1201
00:53:04,848 --> 00:53:06,892
‪I do have a lot of coins,

1202
00:53:06,975 --> 00:53:09,477
‪but I honestly didn't win
‪the bid last round.

1203
00:53:09,561 --> 00:53:10,729
‪-You didn't?
‪-I bid one won.

1204
00:53:10,812 --> 00:53:12,564
‪-You did?
‪-All I have are two triangles.

1205
00:53:12,647 --> 00:53:14,608
‪-Please keep this between us.
‪-Of course.

1206
00:53:14,691 --> 00:53:16,151
‪Here's what I'm more curious about.

1207
00:53:16,234 --> 00:53:17,694
‪Are we not doing the giant-killing?

1208
00:53:17,777 --> 00:53:19,821
‪-What?
‪-Have you called off the giant-killing?

1209
00:53:19,905 --> 00:53:20,989
‪Just be honest with me.

1210
00:53:21,072 --> 00:53:22,908
‪-This game is made to take him down.
‪-Look.

1211
00:53:22,991 --> 00:53:25,619
‪Dong-min is incredibly smart.

1212
00:53:25,702 --> 00:53:30,206
‪-He knows I'm coming for him.
‪-Right.

1213
00:53:30,290 --> 00:53:32,792
‪So I believe he can come up with
‪numerous escape plans.

1214
00:53:32,876 --> 00:53:36,922
‪But we have the overwhelming lead
‪just in coin count alone.

1215
00:53:37,005 --> 00:53:41,009
‪Unless Dong-min dumps 20 or more
‪into 1 shape at once,

1216
00:53:41,092 --> 00:53:44,721
‪if we use 15 each on what he's bidding,
‪we can make sure he doesn't get anything.

1217
00:53:44,804 --> 00:53:46,556
‪I'll definitely block him at least once.

1218
00:53:47,057 --> 00:53:50,018
‪But there's no way
‪I can block him in all seven rounds.

1219
00:53:50,101 --> 00:53:53,104
‪So the rest of you need to decide.

1220
00:53:53,188 --> 00:53:54,606
‪I can only provide information.

1221
00:53:55,273 --> 00:53:59,611
‪Honestly, I was more of a spy
‪than part of the leadership.

1222
00:53:59,694 --> 00:54:02,238
‪I thought the leadership would be solid,

1223
00:54:02,322 --> 00:54:04,574
‪but ORBIT turned out to be more peculiar
‪than I expected.

1224
00:54:04,658 --> 00:54:06,368
<i>‪I just couldn't get a read on him.</i>

1225
00:54:09,412 --> 00:54:11,206
‪What's up?

1226
00:54:11,289 --> 00:54:12,624
‪Are we not gonna talk?

1227
00:54:12,707 --> 00:54:14,167
‪We're both going for the star.

1228
00:54:14,250 --> 00:54:16,211
‪Are we just doing whatever
‪without talking?

1229
00:54:16,294 --> 00:54:17,545
‪Yeah.

1230
00:54:19,297 --> 00:54:22,467
‪I figured he'd at least wanna talk,
‪but he didn't even come looking for me.

1231
00:54:22,550 --> 00:54:24,302
‪He was busy chatting with others.

1232
00:54:24,386 --> 00:54:27,097
<i>‪I assumed he must be planning</i>
<i>‪to bid high to box me out.</i>

1233
00:54:27,180 --> 00:54:31,643
‪So I figured bidding one or two won
‪would be more efficient.

1234
00:54:33,269 --> 00:54:36,064
‪You have bid one two-won coin.

1235
00:54:36,648 --> 00:54:38,233
‪Should I go big on this?

1236
00:54:39,943 --> 00:54:42,362
‪If I use two Pieces, how much can I spend?

1237
00:54:44,280 --> 00:54:46,074
‪I'll bid 16 won.

1238
00:54:46,157 --> 00:54:48,201
‪You have bid 16 won in total.

1239
00:54:51,871 --> 00:54:54,290
‪-Can I talk to John for a bit?
‪-Sure.

1240
00:54:56,918 --> 00:54:58,920
‪-This is our first chat ever.
‪-I know.

1241
00:54:59,421 --> 00:55:02,090
‪I just wanna talk about one thing.

1242
00:55:02,173 --> 00:55:04,551
‪Because of ORBIT's targeting,

1243
00:55:05,135 --> 00:55:06,845
‪I don't even have a sliver of hope.

1244
00:55:08,096 --> 00:55:09,097
‪But…

1245
00:55:09,889 --> 00:55:11,307
‪I still have a chance.

1246
00:55:11,391 --> 00:55:14,561
‪What I think is possible is that

1247
00:55:14,644 --> 00:55:18,064
‪if I do decent in this round,

1248
00:55:19,107 --> 00:55:20,108
‪I can come in first.

1249
00:55:20,191 --> 00:55:21,985
‪-Okay.
‪-If this round works out.

1250
00:55:22,068 --> 00:55:23,445
‪I'm telling you this in confidence.

1251
00:55:23,528 --> 00:55:27,657
‪After this round, I don't know
‪if a chance like this will come again.

1252
00:55:27,741 --> 00:55:31,286
‪Starting next round,
‪I'll make sure you don't come in last.

1253
00:55:31,870 --> 00:55:34,622
‪And after that,
‪I'll give you the alliance token.

1254
00:55:36,916 --> 00:55:38,501
‪So you're aiming for first place?

1255
00:55:38,585 --> 00:55:40,253
‪That's the only way.

1256
00:55:40,336 --> 00:55:41,421
‪That's it.

1257
00:55:41,504 --> 00:55:44,049
‪Then there's nothing I can do for you.

1258
00:55:44,549 --> 00:55:47,427
‪-I'm just making you an offer.
‪-I understand.

1259
00:55:47,510 --> 00:55:51,514
‪If you were at risk of coming in last,

1260
00:55:51,598 --> 00:55:52,891
‪then honestly, I'd…

1261
00:55:53,391 --> 00:55:55,602
‪I haven't gotten anything so far.

1262
00:55:56,186 --> 00:55:57,395
‪That's not true.

1263
00:55:58,271 --> 00:55:59,481
‪-You didn't get the stars?
‪-No.

1264
00:56:01,107 --> 00:56:03,777
‪I figured I'd be targeted
‪in Rounds 1 and 2,

1265
00:56:03,860 --> 00:56:05,612
‪so I only bid one won.

1266
00:56:06,237 --> 00:56:08,948
‪If I don't win the circle bid this time,

1267
00:56:09,032 --> 00:56:11,701
‪I'll be done for.

1268
00:56:13,119 --> 00:56:17,582
<i>‪I thought about</i>
<i>‪why </i><i>‪Dong-min </i><i>‪would say that to me.</i>

1269
00:56:17,665 --> 00:56:22,629
‪I don't think he came to me
‪thinking I'd fall for it.

1270
00:56:22,712 --> 00:56:26,299
<i>‪It felt more like a bluff,</i>
<i>‪like "I'm gonna bid this much."</i>

1271
00:56:26,382 --> 00:56:28,259
<i>‪"So you should spend as much as </i><i>‪you </i><i>‪can."</i>

1272
00:56:28,343 --> 00:56:30,178
‪That's how I understood it.

1273
00:56:30,678 --> 00:56:32,180
‪Dong-min told me

1274
00:56:32,806 --> 00:56:34,724
‪that he only bid one won both rounds.

1275
00:56:34,808 --> 00:56:37,685
‪-That doesn't add up.
‪-Kyung-lyul bid three won.

1276
00:56:37,769 --> 00:56:41,314
‪We also bid three won for the triangle,
‪then there should've been two secrets.

1277
00:56:41,397 --> 00:56:44,734
‪-That makes no sense.
‪-Dong-min must've spent a ton here.

1278
00:56:44,818 --> 00:56:49,155
‪He was certain that we bid high.
‪He had no idea we'd bid three.

1279
00:56:49,239 --> 00:56:50,949
‪So he bid a lot. I'd say at least…

1280
00:56:51,032 --> 00:56:52,283
‪-Over four.
‪-Right.

1281
00:56:52,367 --> 00:56:55,036
‪-No, I think he bid at least ten won.
‪-Yeah, I think so too.

1282
00:56:55,120 --> 00:56:59,499
‪He said he's determined
‪to win big this round.

1283
00:56:59,582 --> 00:57:01,000
‪-Four circles?
‪-All of them.

1284
00:57:01,084 --> 00:57:02,877
‪Yeah, but that's a lie too.

1285
00:57:02,961 --> 00:57:06,422
‪-Yurisa, I talked to him.
‪-Yes? I'm listening.

1286
00:57:06,506 --> 00:57:08,716
‪-I'll leave this to your judgment.
‪-Okay.

1287
00:57:08,800 --> 00:57:10,468
‪-John…
‪-Yes?

1288
00:57:10,552 --> 00:57:11,678
‪He's going in big.

1289
00:57:11,761 --> 00:57:13,638
‪Going in big? How big?

1290
00:57:13,721 --> 00:57:16,099
‪-I told him I'm going all out this round.
‪-Do you know?

1291
00:57:16,182 --> 00:57:17,934
‪-When I did,
‪-Yes?

1292
00:57:18,017 --> 00:57:20,603
‪he said, "Sorry, but I have to as well."

1293
00:57:20,687 --> 00:57:23,648
‪I have 29 won right now.

1294
00:57:24,482 --> 00:57:27,068
‪-Then I'll bid the minimum this time.
‪-Okay.

1295
00:57:27,152 --> 00:57:29,779
‪-You go big and take it.
‪-Okay.

1296
00:57:29,863 --> 00:57:33,408
‪So far, he has used
‪his one-won and three-won coins.

1297
00:57:33,491 --> 00:57:36,411
‪-Right.
‪-There's a chance he could go up to 18.

1298
00:57:37,078 --> 00:57:38,788
‪Seventeen?

1299
00:57:38,872 --> 00:57:40,081
‪Eighteen?

1300
00:57:43,543 --> 00:57:44,794
‪One one-won coin.

1301
00:57:45,462 --> 00:57:48,089
‪-They'll hear you.
‪-You have bid one won.

1302
00:57:49,966 --> 00:57:52,260
‪-You have bid one one-won coin.
‪-Yes.

1303
00:57:54,846 --> 00:57:59,017
‪You have bid one ten-won coin,
‪one five-won coin, and two two-won coins,

1304
00:57:59,100 --> 00:58:01,644
‪totaling 19 won.

1305
00:58:06,316 --> 00:58:08,109
‪John Park, please submit your coins.

1306
00:58:12,906 --> 00:58:14,657
‪I'll bid 19 won.

1307
00:58:14,741 --> 00:58:18,578
‪One ten-won coin,
‪one five-won coin, two two-won coins.

1308
00:58:19,954 --> 00:58:21,789
<i>‪Bidding is now complete.</i>

1309
00:58:22,457 --> 00:58:25,585
<i>‪Here is the winning bid for each shape.</i>

1310
00:58:25,668 --> 00:58:27,795
‪△: 7 WON, ◯: SECRET, ☆: 16 WON

1311
00:58:27,879 --> 00:58:29,839
‪No way. The circle went for more than 16?

1312
00:58:29,923 --> 00:58:31,257
‪The star went for 16?

1313
00:58:31,758 --> 00:58:33,343
‪-Did you bid 16?
‪-Yes.

1314
00:58:33,843 --> 00:58:36,554
‪-That secret is nuts.
‪-Man, that's crazy.

1315
00:58:36,638 --> 00:58:39,474
‪Wow, so the secret must be…

1316
00:58:39,557 --> 00:58:41,935
‪-What's the seven about?
‪-I guess you didn't trust me.

1317
00:58:42,018 --> 00:58:43,102
‪I really bid one won.

1318
00:58:43,937 --> 00:58:45,939
‪Why'd you spend so much?

1319
00:58:46,022 --> 00:58:48,191
<i>‪Round 4 will now begin.</i>

1320
00:58:48,274 --> 00:58:50,193
‪-You probably got it.
‪-Right.

1321
00:58:50,276 --> 00:58:54,239
‪-So you won 4 circles in Round 3.
‪-That's right.

1322
00:58:54,322 --> 00:58:57,534
<i>‪When we calculated everyone's coin count,</i>

1323
00:58:57,617 --> 00:59:01,746
‪18 won was the maximum John could bid.

1324
00:59:01,829 --> 00:59:07,627
‪That's why I bid 19 to be safe.
‪So I think it's safe to assume I won that.

1325
00:59:07,710 --> 00:59:10,588
‪You might as well act like you didn't.

1326
00:59:10,672 --> 00:59:12,549
‪-That'd be better.
‪-That's what I've been doing.

1327
00:59:12,632 --> 00:59:16,844
‪I won the circle bid,
‪but I kept telling everyone I lost it.

1328
00:59:16,928 --> 00:59:19,722
<i>‪I've been saying I'm in last place</i>
<i>‪with no shapes so far.</i>

1329
00:59:19,806 --> 00:59:21,724
‪I'm in last place.

1330
00:59:21,808 --> 00:59:23,560
‪Yurisa, what have you won?

1331
00:59:23,643 --> 00:59:24,936
‪-Nothing, right?
‪-Nothing.

1332
00:59:25,019 --> 00:59:26,396
‪-Please help me.
‪-There she goes.

1333
00:59:26,479 --> 00:59:27,397
‪Please give me some money.

1334
00:59:27,480 --> 00:59:29,148
‪Seriously?

1335
00:59:29,232 --> 00:59:30,108
‪Come on now.

1336
00:59:31,192 --> 00:59:32,860
‪I wanna go for the star.

1337
00:59:32,944 --> 00:59:34,070
‪I wanna too.

1338
00:59:34,153 --> 00:59:36,114
‪If you're definitely going for it,
‪then I'll sit out.

1339
00:59:36,197 --> 00:59:38,700
‪-That might be best. Three will be tricky.
‪-All right.

1340
00:59:38,783 --> 00:59:41,119
‪Then I guess I'll go for the circle.

1341
00:59:44,789 --> 00:59:48,167
‪Anyone need anything specific?

1342
00:59:48,251 --> 00:59:50,128
‪-You all have triangles, right?
‪-I need stars.

1343
00:59:50,211 --> 00:59:52,422
‪I need circles.

1344
00:59:52,922 --> 00:59:55,800
‪-Then…
‪-I also need circles.

1345
00:59:56,467 --> 00:59:58,344
‪Then I'll go for the triangle.

1346
00:59:58,428 --> 00:59:59,679
‪You're all good on the triangle, yeah?

1347
00:59:59,762 --> 01:00:02,640
‪-Yeah, I'm set.
‪-He'll follow me again anyway.

1348
01:00:08,271 --> 01:00:10,773
‪You really need to shut down
‪the triangle bid this time.

1349
01:00:10,857 --> 01:00:12,942
‪Yeah, I'm planning to.

1350
01:00:21,159 --> 01:00:23,536
‪If Dong-min keeps getting targeted,
‪there's no way for him to survive.

1351
01:00:23,620 --> 01:00:26,914
‪ORBIT isn't really going after him
‪as much as you think.

1352
01:00:26,998 --> 01:00:29,626
‪He says he's gonna go all in just once,

1353
01:00:29,709 --> 01:00:32,712
‪turning this into a mind game
‪where you have to anticipate that strike.

1354
01:00:35,757 --> 01:00:38,176
‪If Yurisa chooses that,
‪I guess we're leaving Kyung-lyul alone?

1355
01:00:38,259 --> 01:00:39,552
‪-We have to block him.
‪-How?

1356
01:00:39,636 --> 01:00:40,595
‪-You have to go.
‪-Me?

1357
01:00:40,678 --> 01:00:42,889
‪-Okay, then I'll go after him.
‪-Right.

1358
01:00:42,972 --> 01:00:44,349
‪I'll do the same thing as before.

1359
01:00:46,059 --> 01:00:47,143
‪Just let us all see.

1360
01:00:47,226 --> 01:00:48,394
‪Okay.

1361
01:00:48,478 --> 01:00:49,604
‪Star? Okay.

1362
01:00:56,444 --> 01:00:57,403
‪Circle.

1363
01:00:58,529 --> 01:01:00,448
‪I've got nowhere to go.

1364
01:01:00,948 --> 01:01:02,075
‪Should I go for the triangle?

1365
01:01:02,158 --> 01:01:03,701
‪ORBIT and Dong-min
‪already went for the triangle.

1366
01:01:03,785 --> 01:01:05,203
‪Kyung-lyul and Dong-jae went for the star.

1367
01:01:05,286 --> 01:01:06,788
‪-It's a battleground everywhere.
‪-I know.

1368
01:01:06,871 --> 01:01:08,039
‪-You should--
‪-Support me

1369
01:01:08,122 --> 01:01:09,582
‪if this is your throwaway round.

1370
01:01:09,666 --> 01:01:11,626
‪-Go with the star. I'll go for the circle.
‪-Yeah, do that.

1371
01:01:11,709 --> 01:01:13,961
‪The star already has two bidders.

1372
01:01:14,671 --> 01:01:16,673
<i>‪Shape selection is now closed.</i>

1373
01:01:17,173 --> 01:01:20,051
<i>‪Here are the shapes</i>
<i>‪each </i><i>‪player </i><i>‪has </i><i>‪selected.</i>

1374
01:01:20,677 --> 01:01:21,969
‪Oh boy.

1375
01:01:22,053 --> 01:01:23,721
<i>‪Bidding will now begin.</i>

1376
01:01:24,222 --> 01:01:26,224
‪Do you want all the circles,

1377
01:01:26,307 --> 01:01:28,851
‪or are you willing to share?

1378
01:01:28,935 --> 01:01:31,229
‪I think we can work something out.

1379
01:01:31,312 --> 01:01:33,189
‪We can both bid one or two won.

1380
01:01:33,272 --> 01:01:35,191
‪If you don't have one won,

1381
01:01:35,274 --> 01:01:37,735
‪-you'll have to use a Piece.
‪-I have it, and I'm open to using Pieces.

1382
01:01:37,819 --> 01:01:40,363
‪If you're okay with it,
‪I'd prefer to go for two.

1383
01:01:40,446 --> 01:01:42,407
‪-Then, two won each?
‪-Go with two?

1384
01:01:42,490 --> 01:01:43,491
‪-Two.
‪-Okay.

1385
01:01:45,034 --> 01:01:47,453
‪Jung Won-young, please submit your coins.

1386
01:01:48,871 --> 01:01:50,081
‪One two-won coin.

1387
01:01:50,164 --> 01:01:51,541
‪Please submit your coins.

1388
01:01:52,417 --> 01:01:53,334
‪I'll bid four won.

1389
01:01:55,878 --> 01:01:57,630
‪You have bid four won in total.

1390
01:02:01,592 --> 01:02:03,177
‪-This--
‪-No need to fight, right?

1391
01:02:03,845 --> 01:02:05,263
‪-But--
‪-Are you gonna block?

1392
01:02:05,346 --> 01:02:08,391
‪It'd be good for me to win it too.
‪I need to go for it.

1393
01:02:08,474 --> 01:02:10,977
‪I'm just gonna bid one won.

1394
01:02:11,978 --> 01:02:14,230
‪You have bid one one-won coin.

1395
01:02:14,814 --> 01:02:16,357
‪Are you gonna bid a lot?

1396
01:02:16,441 --> 01:02:18,109
‪-What?
‪-I'm not gonna.

1397
01:02:18,192 --> 01:02:19,736
‪So how much exactly?

1398
01:02:19,819 --> 01:02:20,820
‪I don't know yet.

1399
01:02:20,903 --> 01:02:24,449
‪But I don't really need it
‪that badly either.

1400
01:02:24,532 --> 01:02:27,034
‪Then we can each get one.

1401
01:02:27,118 --> 01:02:28,453
‪Yeah, that'd be nice.

1402
01:02:29,036 --> 01:02:30,580
‪I'll bid three won.

1403
01:02:30,663 --> 01:02:33,332
‪You have bid one three-won coin.

1404
01:02:35,042 --> 01:02:37,170
‪I'm bidding 12 won.

1405
01:02:37,253 --> 01:02:39,297
‪You have bid 12 won in total.

1406
01:02:43,384 --> 01:02:44,844
‪Yurisa's in danger.

1407
01:02:44,927 --> 01:02:46,179
‪-No, she's fine.
‪-She hasn't gotten anything.

1408
01:02:46,262 --> 01:02:48,514
‪-What?
‪-She said she has nothing.

1409
01:02:49,098 --> 01:02:50,725
‪-We're moving into Round 5 now, right?
‪-ORBIT.

1410
01:02:50,808 --> 01:02:52,435
‪-You have nothing, right?
‪-Yeah.

1411
01:02:52,518 --> 01:02:55,313
‪-Right, then you're in big trouble.
‪-I'm in dead last.

1412
01:02:55,396 --> 01:02:57,607
‪-Yurisa, if that's the case…
‪-Yes?

1413
01:02:57,690 --> 01:02:59,317
‪-Sorry, can you give us a second?
‪-Sure.

1414
01:03:01,319 --> 01:03:02,528
‪Let's see.

1415
01:03:03,696 --> 01:03:06,699
‪If I don't win anything this round,
‪I could end up coming in last.

1416
01:03:06,783 --> 01:03:09,744
‪-So I'll win this bid.
‪-Okay.

1417
01:03:09,827 --> 01:03:12,371
‪I'll do whatever I can to block ORBIT

1418
01:03:12,455 --> 01:03:13,623
‪-and win the bid.
‪-Okay.

1419
01:03:15,458 --> 01:03:17,919
‪You have bid one one-won coin.

1420
01:03:19,295 --> 01:03:21,339
‪Jang Dong-min, please submit your coins.

1421
01:03:22,381 --> 01:03:23,674
‪I've got six…

1422
01:03:24,675 --> 01:03:26,052
‪Yurisa.

1423
01:03:27,053 --> 01:03:29,222
‪Are you just gonna end the week
‪having done nothing but backing Dong-min?

1424
01:03:29,305 --> 01:03:30,264
‪Seems that way.

1425
01:03:31,432 --> 01:03:33,017
‪-No, come on.
‪-It seems that way.

1426
01:03:33,100 --> 01:03:34,268
‪Please submit your coins.

1427
01:03:34,352 --> 01:03:35,186
‪Sure.

1428
01:03:39,440 --> 01:03:41,192
<i>‪Bidding is now complete.</i>

1429
01:03:41,818 --> 01:03:44,320
<i>‪Here is the winning bid for each </i><i>‪shape.</i>

1430
01:03:45,696 --> 01:03:47,114
‪The winning bid for the triangle
‪was two won?

1431
01:03:47,198 --> 01:03:48,324
‪△: 2 WON, ◯: 4 WON, ☆: SECRET

1432
01:03:48,407 --> 01:03:49,784
‪Why so cheap?

1433
01:03:51,202 --> 01:03:52,662
‪Did Dong-min sweep it all?

1434
01:03:52,745 --> 01:03:53,913
‪Damn it.

1435
01:03:53,996 --> 01:03:55,122
‪What did ORBIT do?

1436
01:03:55,206 --> 01:03:56,791
‪Hold on, ORBIT.

1437
01:03:56,874 --> 01:03:57,834
‪ORBIT.

1438
01:03:59,126 --> 01:04:03,214
‪ORBIT was originally
‪supposed to keep Dong-min in check.

1439
01:04:03,297 --> 01:04:07,844
<i>‪But when we saw the results,</i>
<i>‪the numbers made no sense.</i>

1440
01:04:07,927 --> 01:04:09,428
<i>‪Just two won for the triangle?</i>

1441
01:04:09,512 --> 01:04:11,055
<i>‪It was a bid between ORBIT,</i>
<i>‪Dong-min, and Yurisa.</i>

1442
01:04:11,138 --> 01:04:13,057
‪What on earth did ORBIT do?

1443
01:04:13,641 --> 01:04:15,393
‪Man, he got it for just two won.

1444
01:04:15,977 --> 01:04:17,311
‪Why didn't you stop him?

1445
01:04:17,395 --> 01:04:18,896
‪-What?
‪-What game were you playing?

1446
01:04:18,980 --> 01:04:20,231
‪-Huh?
‪-Why didn't you step in?

1447
01:04:20,314 --> 01:04:21,440
‪You didn't step in for the triangle bid.

1448
01:04:21,524 --> 01:04:23,150
‪What's going on?

1449
01:04:25,486 --> 01:04:27,655
‪But you got two stars.

1450
01:04:28,239 --> 01:04:29,866
‪How much do you think I bid?

1451
01:04:29,949 --> 01:04:32,159
‪-I won with 12 won.
‪-You did?

1452
01:04:33,160 --> 01:04:36,873
‪That's how stressed out I am right now.

1453
01:04:36,956 --> 01:04:40,334
‪I don't want it to be like this
‪when going up against you.

1454
01:04:40,418 --> 01:04:42,295
‪We should just be fighting together.

1455
01:04:42,378 --> 01:04:45,548
‪This is basically
‪you fighting seven players.

1456
01:04:45,631 --> 01:04:47,758
‪Do you believe
‪those three players are on your side?

1457
01:04:47,842 --> 01:04:49,093
‪They're all targeting you
‪to send you home.

1458
01:04:49,176 --> 01:04:51,053
‪-That's the only way they can win.
‪-I know that.

1459
01:04:51,137 --> 01:04:52,972
‪We have to make sure
‪Dong-min comes in last.

1460
01:04:53,055 --> 01:04:55,016
‪-First, I think Dong-min…
‪-We must keep him in check.

1461
01:04:55,099 --> 01:04:56,559
‪Is your plan to take down Dong-min?

1462
01:04:56,642 --> 01:04:58,686
‪So as always,

1463
01:04:58,769 --> 01:05:00,479
‪I'm on the side of whoever's cornered.

1464
01:05:00,563 --> 01:05:02,356
‪You're already fighting seven people.

1465
01:05:02,440 --> 01:05:05,151
‪Things must've been so tough for you.

1466
01:05:05,234 --> 01:05:06,694
‪I bet they were all targeting you.

1467
01:05:06,777 --> 01:05:10,781
‪The way I see it,
‪if it's Dong-min against seven,

1468
01:05:10,865 --> 01:05:13,367
‪then he's someone
‪who needs protection too.

1469
01:05:13,451 --> 01:05:18,372
‪His sympathy for me will grow
‪if he sees me as weak.

1470
01:05:18,456 --> 01:05:22,335
‪But this is all part of
‪my high-level mind game.

1471
01:05:26,213 --> 01:05:29,717
‪You have bid one five-won coin
‪and one one-won coin, totaling six won.

1472
01:05:29,800 --> 01:05:32,136
‪-I won with 12 won.
‪-You did?

1473
01:05:33,012 --> 01:05:34,847
‪-You can dodge four rounds right now.
‪-Yeah.

1474
01:05:34,931 --> 01:05:37,850
‪The reality is, there are three rounds
‪where I have to chase you.

1475
01:05:37,934 --> 01:05:40,478
‪So play cautiously for those four rounds,

1476
01:05:40,561 --> 01:05:43,439
‪and I'll just bid one
‪in the other three rounds.

1477
01:05:47,902 --> 01:05:50,404
‪You really need to shut down
‪the triangle bid this time.

1478
01:05:50,488 --> 01:05:51,572
‪Yeah, I'm planning to.

1479
01:05:52,073 --> 01:05:52,907
‪Just bid one.

1480
01:05:52,990 --> 01:05:54,241
‪-You wanna win this round?
‪-Yeah.

1481
01:05:55,826 --> 01:05:57,411
‪-Done.
‪-One one-won coin.

1482
01:05:57,495 --> 01:05:58,329
‪Thank you.

1483
01:05:58,913 --> 01:06:00,581
‪I must have faith.

1484
01:06:02,208 --> 01:06:04,460
‪You have bid one two-won coin.

1485
01:06:04,543 --> 01:06:07,171
‪I wanna win today
‪in a way that makes people think,

1486
01:06:07,672 --> 01:06:11,175
<i>‪"He's a monster who comes out on top,</i>
<i>‪no matter what you throw at him."</i>

1487
01:06:11,759 --> 01:06:14,428
‪-What happened?
‪-We couldn't have blocked this one.

1488
01:06:14,512 --> 01:06:16,764
‪-Why not?
‪-All you had to do was bid three won.

1489
01:06:16,847 --> 01:06:19,558
‪Even if you had to let him win,
‪you should've made him spend his coins.

1490
01:06:19,642 --> 01:06:20,810
‪Two is ridiculous.

1491
01:06:20,893 --> 01:06:22,770
‪You obviously let him have it

1492
01:06:22,853 --> 01:06:24,355
‪-after a discussion.
‪-Think about it.

1493
01:06:24,438 --> 01:06:26,857
‪We only get three chances to block him.

1494
01:06:26,941 --> 01:06:28,192
‪-Listen.
‪-So why--

1495
01:06:28,275 --> 01:06:30,403
‪Dong-min just won

1496
01:06:30,486 --> 01:06:32,822
‪the triangle bid this round.

1497
01:06:32,905 --> 01:06:34,490
‪Right? And maybe the stars earlier.

1498
01:06:34,573 --> 01:06:35,408
‪He did.

1499
01:06:35,491 --> 01:06:37,702
‪So now Dong-min
‪has stars and triangles. That's it.

1500
01:06:37,785 --> 01:06:39,412
‪That's not what we're asking.

1501
01:06:39,495 --> 01:06:41,872
‪Why did you agree to help him out
‪in the first place?

1502
01:06:41,956 --> 01:06:43,582
‪A turn where someone wins
‪three triangles at once,

1503
01:06:43,666 --> 01:06:46,043
‪or two stars at once,
‪or four circles at once?

1504
01:06:46,127 --> 01:06:48,462
‪That's an incredibly powerful round.

1505
01:06:48,546 --> 01:06:49,630
‪I managed one of them,

1506
01:06:49,714 --> 01:06:53,259
<i>‪and it took me 14 won</i>
<i>‪to win 3 triangles in Round 2.</i>

1507
01:06:53,759 --> 01:06:56,178
<i>‪But Dong-min took three triangles</i>
<i>‪for only two won.</i>

1508
01:06:56,262 --> 01:06:58,723
‪He managed to make
‪a very powerful move for a very low price.

1509
01:06:58,806 --> 01:07:01,267
‪I mean, why can't I work with him?

1510
01:07:01,350 --> 01:07:04,979
‪-Right, so what was the deal?
‪-But why? Why did you decide to do that?

1511
01:07:05,062 --> 01:07:09,233
‪-Taking down Dong-min was never my goal.
‪-Okay.

1512
01:07:09,316 --> 01:07:11,277
‪Making a specific person the winner
‪was never my goal either.

1513
01:07:11,360 --> 01:07:13,654
‪-But you just made Dong-min the winner.
‪-No.

1514
01:07:13,738 --> 01:07:15,364
‪I won't make him the winner.

1515
01:07:15,448 --> 01:07:16,907
‪I'll make sure of that, starting now.

1516
01:07:16,991 --> 01:07:19,535
‪But Dong-min also had nothing.

1517
01:07:19,618 --> 01:07:21,579
‪-That's why I wanted him to win, and--
‪-What are you talking about?

1518
01:07:21,662 --> 01:07:23,080
‪You knew he got two stars.

1519
01:07:23,164 --> 01:07:25,082
‪Right. John, you're done, right?

1520
01:07:25,166 --> 01:07:26,375
‪You got everything you need, yeah?

1521
01:07:26,459 --> 01:07:28,085
‪Just say what you need to say.

1522
01:07:28,169 --> 01:07:31,172
‪Explain why you decided to work with him.

1523
01:07:31,255 --> 01:07:34,050
‪You just served him three triangles
‪on a silver platter.

1524
01:07:34,133 --> 01:07:37,344
‪Yurisa and Dong-min are allies
‪who communicate easily.

1525
01:07:37,428 --> 01:07:39,638
‪And you just happened
‪to be there with them.

1526
01:07:39,722 --> 01:07:40,931
‪Right, in that situation--

1527
01:07:41,015 --> 01:07:42,767
‪-So, for example--
‪-Hear me out.

1528
01:07:42,850 --> 01:07:44,518
‪If it were one person from our team
‪and one from theirs

1529
01:07:44,602 --> 01:07:46,395
‪and you joined them and bid one won,

1530
01:07:46,479 --> 01:07:47,855
‪-I'd be fine with that.
‪-As I said,

1531
01:07:47,938 --> 01:07:49,440
‪I'm not trying to help one person.

1532
01:07:49,523 --> 01:07:51,484
‪But you just did.

1533
01:07:51,567 --> 01:07:53,986
‪I worked with him
‪for just one out of four rounds.

1534
01:07:54,070 --> 01:07:56,280
‪-Okay, we get that.
‪-Right?

1535
01:07:56,363 --> 01:08:00,201
‪But it only makes sense that we're angry
‪because we were caught off guard.

1536
01:08:00,284 --> 01:08:02,495
‪And it's highly unlikely
‪we'll be able to hinder him

1537
01:08:02,578 --> 01:08:03,954
‪in the next three rounds.

1538
01:08:04,038 --> 01:08:06,582
‪He swept the triangles
‪so easily and efficiently.

1539
01:08:06,665 --> 01:08:08,125
‪If you think about it,

1540
01:08:08,209 --> 01:08:11,253
‪Dong-min can just bide his time
‪and go all in on one turn.

1541
01:08:11,337 --> 01:08:12,755
‪How are you gonna stop that?

1542
01:08:12,838 --> 01:08:14,465
‪You have a one-in-three chance.

1543
01:08:14,548 --> 01:08:15,382
‪But listen.

1544
01:08:15,466 --> 01:08:18,552
‪It may look that way
‪when your sole focus is on Dong-min.

1545
01:08:18,636 --> 01:08:20,763
‪But the three of you
‪are in a pretty good place.

1546
01:08:20,846 --> 01:08:24,183
‪-That's not what we're talking about.
‪-Hold on.

1547
01:08:24,266 --> 01:08:26,560
‪-You're trying to find a balance.
‪-And that's fine.

1548
01:08:26,644 --> 01:08:29,188
‪But the scales were leaning their way
‪long before you got here.

1549
01:08:29,271 --> 01:08:30,523
‪That's the situation.

1550
01:08:30,606 --> 01:08:33,526
‪By serving him three triangles
‪with your one-won bid,

1551
01:08:33,609 --> 01:08:34,902
‪you as good as handed him the win.

1552
01:08:34,985 --> 01:08:36,737
‪I'll be playing solo from now on.

1553
01:08:36,821 --> 01:08:38,239
‪I just don't get it.

1554
01:08:38,322 --> 01:08:41,158
‪I could've understood
‪if you had done this to win yourself.

1555
01:08:41,242 --> 01:08:45,788
‪But from where we stand, you just did this
‪because you wanted Dong-min to win.

1556
01:08:51,460 --> 01:08:52,962
‪I'm so pissed off.

1557
01:08:53,045 --> 01:08:57,216
‪ORBIT was playing in a way
‪that made absolutely no sense.

1558
01:08:57,299 --> 01:09:00,970
<i>‪I spent a lot to win the 4 circles</i>
<i>‪in Round 3.</i>

1559
01:09:01,053 --> 01:09:03,097
‪There are no more plays
‪I can make at this point.

1560
01:09:03,180 --> 01:09:05,975
<i>‪So there was no reason</i>
<i>‪to discuss it with the others.</i>

1561
01:09:06,058 --> 01:09:09,311
‪And it looks like
‪everyone's playing solo now.

1562
01:09:09,395 --> 01:09:10,229
‪So I just left.

1563
01:09:10,729 --> 01:09:13,315
‪So you're saying
‪you're helping everyone out, right?

1564
01:09:13,399 --> 01:09:14,650
‪You can't put it like that.

1565
01:09:14,733 --> 01:09:18,028
‪I'm looking to swap the players
‪in the living area and prison.

1566
01:09:18,112 --> 01:09:21,740
‪But that doesn't necessarily mean
‪I wanna destroy Dong-min.

1567
01:09:21,824 --> 01:09:23,284
‪Does anyone need circles?

1568
01:09:23,367 --> 01:09:25,286
‪-I do.
‪-Okay.

1569
01:09:25,369 --> 01:09:28,122
‪I just need two circles
‪and one triangle to fill my board.

1570
01:09:28,205 --> 01:09:30,291
‪-You need to win this at least.
‪-The triangle?

1571
01:09:30,374 --> 01:09:31,750
‪-Should I go for the triangle?
‪-Yeah.

1572
01:09:31,834 --> 01:09:34,128
‪Kyung-lyul hasn't won any triangles yet.

1573
01:09:34,211 --> 01:09:36,005
‪-He'll make a bid for it.
‪-None.

1574
01:09:36,088 --> 01:09:36,964
‪Triangle.

1575
01:09:39,758 --> 01:09:40,968
‪The way I see it,

1576
01:09:41,051 --> 01:09:42,803
‪in Rounds 6 and 7,

1577
01:09:42,887 --> 01:09:45,181
‪ORBIT will bid on what I bid,
‪no matter what.

1578
01:09:45,264 --> 01:09:48,058
‪You go for the circle in those rounds.

1579
01:09:48,142 --> 01:09:50,769
‪If I do that,

1580
01:09:51,478 --> 01:09:53,063
‪then I'll be totally screwed,

1581
01:09:53,147 --> 01:09:55,608
‪because ORBIT could just go for the circle
‪in those rounds.

1582
01:09:55,691 --> 01:09:57,276
‪He's gonna follow me.

1583
01:09:57,359 --> 01:09:59,028
‪-Really?
‪-Yeah, no matter what.

1584
01:09:59,111 --> 01:10:01,113
‪-He's been doing that from the start.
‪-Right.

1585
01:10:01,197 --> 01:10:03,032
‪So you don't have to worry about that.

1586
01:10:03,115 --> 01:10:05,367
‪Then I'll go for the circle in Round 5.

1587
01:10:05,451 --> 01:10:06,952
<i>‪Three minutes remaining.</i>

1588
01:10:07,453 --> 01:10:09,121
‪We're in Round 5 now.

1589
01:10:09,205 --> 01:10:10,873
‪You need to go first.

1590
01:10:13,918 --> 01:10:17,129
<i>‪-I'm a star</i>
‪-Star.

1591
01:10:19,256 --> 01:10:20,841
‪-You need to win, right?
‪-No.

1592
01:10:20,925 --> 01:10:22,593
‪We can share it if you wanna.

1593
01:10:32,394 --> 01:10:34,021
‪Then you should go for the circle.

1594
01:10:34,521 --> 01:10:37,441
‪That'd mean they get the star.

1595
01:10:38,067 --> 01:10:39,777
‪We'd just be handing them stars.

1596
01:10:39,860 --> 01:10:41,946
‪They need one star each.

1597
01:10:42,029 --> 01:10:43,781
‪There's no reason
‪they wouldn't work together.

1598
01:10:43,864 --> 01:10:45,574
‪I need to get in there
‪and try to stop them.

1599
01:10:45,658 --> 01:10:48,327
‪We'll just end up losing at this rate.

1600
01:10:48,410 --> 01:10:49,662
‪-Go ahead, then.
‪-Okay.

1601
01:10:53,249 --> 01:10:56,502
‪So it's just you and ORBIT on the circle.

1602
01:10:56,585 --> 01:10:59,171
‪If I go for the circle, he might follow,
‪which would give him one more.

1603
01:10:59,255 --> 01:11:00,422
‪It's fine. That makes sense.

1604
01:11:00,506 --> 01:11:03,133
‪It might be better
‪to let him go for it alone.

1605
01:11:03,217 --> 01:11:04,551
‪He'll only get one.

1606
01:11:04,635 --> 01:11:07,054
‪If Dong-min only gets one circle
‪in the remaining three rounds…

1607
01:11:07,137 --> 01:11:09,556
‪No one selected the circle, right?

1608
01:11:09,640 --> 01:11:10,766
‪Then he can't win.

1609
01:11:10,849 --> 01:11:15,521
‪If I go for the circle at the end
‪and go all in, then I'm guaranteed to win.

1610
01:11:15,604 --> 01:11:16,522
‪That works, right?

1611
01:11:16,605 --> 01:11:17,606
‪Then go for the triangle.

1612
01:11:31,495 --> 01:11:32,621
‪That's weird.

1613
01:11:33,122 --> 01:11:35,040
<i>‪Shape selection is now closed.</i>

1614
01:11:35,582 --> 01:11:38,627
<i>‪Here are the shapes</i>
<i>‪each </i><i>‪player </i><i>‪has </i><i>‪selected.</i>

1615
01:11:38,711 --> 01:11:39,753
‪This is better for us.

1616
01:11:39,837 --> 01:11:41,046
‪He'll only get one.

1617
01:11:41,130 --> 01:11:44,091
‪You got it for one won,
‪so it's not a loss.

1618
01:11:44,174 --> 01:11:49,680
‪If nobody bids on the circle
‪when there are only three rounds left,

1619
01:11:49,763 --> 01:11:51,682
‪that means I can only get one at a time.

1620
01:11:52,516 --> 01:11:55,769
‪So it's not terrible,
‪but it's not great either.

1621
01:11:55,853 --> 01:11:57,813
‪Do the two of you wanna fight for it,

1622
01:11:57,896 --> 01:11:59,690
‪or should we each just take one?

1623
01:11:59,773 --> 01:12:02,234
‪I really don't mind either way.

1624
01:12:02,735 --> 01:12:04,570
‪John Park, please submit your coins.

1625
01:12:06,155 --> 01:12:08,157
‪You have bid one one-won coin.

1626
01:12:08,240 --> 01:12:10,159
‪You need a star, right?

1627
01:12:10,242 --> 01:12:11,660
‪-Yeah.
‪-Just one.

1628
01:12:11,744 --> 01:12:14,413
‪I don't have much filled yet.

1629
01:12:14,496 --> 01:12:18,000
‪But you'd be in a much better spot
‪if I share.

1630
01:12:18,876 --> 01:12:22,421
‪-I need to look out for myself too.
‪-I'll find a way to survive. You take it.

1631
01:12:22,504 --> 01:12:24,048
‪I have to think about my board too.

1632
01:12:24,131 --> 01:12:25,966
‪It's fine.
‪You focus on what you need to do.

1633
01:12:26,508 --> 01:12:27,718
‪Good luck.

1634
01:12:27,801 --> 01:12:29,470
‪Do what you need to do.

1635
01:12:29,553 --> 01:12:31,430
‪If you can't trust me,
‪bid high and win it.

1636
01:12:31,513 --> 01:12:34,600
‪I'll bid two or three.
‪Do whatever you want.

1637
01:12:38,937 --> 01:12:40,356
‪Please submit your coins.

1638
01:12:46,320 --> 01:12:47,237
‪Two Pieces.

1639
01:12:47,321 --> 01:12:48,864
‪-Would you like to exchange your Pieces?
‪-Yes.

1640
01:12:48,947 --> 01:12:51,283
‪And I'll bid five won.

1641
01:12:51,367 --> 01:12:53,243
‪You have bid one five-won coin.

1642
01:12:53,327 --> 01:12:54,244
‪Hold on.

1643
01:12:54,870 --> 01:12:57,623
‪-This too.
‪-You have added one one-won coin.

1644
01:12:57,706 --> 01:13:00,167
‪-Your total bid is six won.
‪-Okay.

1645
01:13:00,751 --> 01:13:02,252
‪Yurisa, you're in the worst spot
‪right now.

1646
01:13:02,336 --> 01:13:04,630
‪-I have nothing, so I must win this time.
‪-Wait.

1647
01:13:04,713 --> 01:13:06,048
‪So you're going all in?

1648
01:13:06,131 --> 01:13:07,716
‪Yeah, I'm gonna use it all up.

1649
01:13:07,800 --> 01:13:10,719
‪-She must have a lot of coins right now.
‪-I do. Almost thirty won.

1650
01:13:10,803 --> 01:13:12,346
‪Right, you've barely used any.

1651
01:13:12,429 --> 01:13:15,140
‪-I have to win the bid this round.
‪-Right.

1652
01:13:15,224 --> 01:13:16,475
‪Anyone set on triangles?

1653
01:13:16,975 --> 01:13:18,602
‪-I chose it because I need some.
‪-So did I.

1654
01:13:20,396 --> 01:13:21,980
‪This is tricky. But you know,

1655
01:13:22,064 --> 01:13:24,441
‪I personally think Yurisa
‪should get to decide.

1656
01:13:24,525 --> 01:13:27,069
‪If she wants to share,

1657
01:13:27,152 --> 01:13:28,737
‪we match that bid and split it up.

1658
01:13:28,821 --> 01:13:31,907
‪The three of us
‪can agree on an amount first.

1659
01:13:31,990 --> 01:13:35,869
‪After what happened in Round 2,
‪I've lost faith in agreements.

1660
01:13:35,953 --> 01:13:37,830
‪-Then--
‪-Can you blame me?

1661
01:13:37,913 --> 01:13:39,665
‪That 3 popped out of nowhere in Round 2.

1662
01:13:39,748 --> 01:13:41,083
‪This is the three-won coin, right?

1663
01:13:42,459 --> 01:13:43,961
‪-I don't get it.
‪-Why would I bid three?

1664
01:13:44,044 --> 01:13:44,878
‪I swear it wasn't me.

1665
01:13:46,880 --> 01:13:49,299
‪There are three rounds left now.

1666
01:13:50,300 --> 01:13:51,969
‪I think eight won should be enough.

1667
01:13:52,052 --> 01:13:53,679
‪-To win the triangle bid?
‪-Yeah.

1668
01:13:53,762 --> 01:13:55,389
‪-Then she should bid nine won.
‪-So Yurisa…

1669
01:13:55,472 --> 01:13:56,306
‪Bid nine?

1670
01:13:56,390 --> 01:13:58,851
‪I'm gonna bid around eight.

1671
01:13:58,934 --> 01:14:01,145
‪Who's he trying to help
‪by bidding eight won?

1672
01:14:01,228 --> 01:14:03,230
‪I genuinely don't understand
‪what he's doing.

1673
01:14:03,313 --> 01:14:05,899
<i>‪The prison and the living area</i>
<i>‪have this narrative going.</i>

1674
01:14:05,983 --> 01:14:07,609
<i>‪If I tear it all down,</i>

1675
01:14:07,693 --> 01:14:11,822
‪I'd become the person
‪who came to destroy <i>‪The Devil's Plan.</i>

1676
01:14:11,905 --> 01:14:15,033
‪I wanna help out somehow,

1677
01:14:15,117 --> 01:14:19,079
‪but with just enough force
‪as a falling snowflake.

1678
01:14:19,163 --> 01:14:22,082
‪It's the same idea as an ion thruster,
‪which in space…

1679
01:14:22,166 --> 01:14:24,418
‪The game gets exciting in the latter half.

1680
01:14:24,501 --> 01:14:26,295
‪Can we talk for a second?

1681
01:14:26,378 --> 01:14:27,546
‪Sure.

1682
01:14:27,629 --> 01:14:31,633
‪ORBIT just came over and said
‪he's definitely gonna bid eight or nine.

1683
01:14:31,717 --> 01:14:34,261
‪So if I wanna take it for myself,

1684
01:14:34,344 --> 01:14:37,306
‪I should either outbid him
‪or give up entirely.

1685
01:14:37,389 --> 01:14:39,349
‪-That's what he said.
‪-Okay.

1686
01:14:40,767 --> 01:14:42,811
‪Can you throw me a lifeline here?

1687
01:14:42,895 --> 01:14:44,146
‪Aren't you fine right now?

1688
01:14:44,229 --> 01:14:45,981
‪-Not at all. I'm really screwed.
‪-Why?

1689
01:14:46,064 --> 01:14:47,107
‪-The thing is…
‪-Why?

1690
01:14:49,485 --> 01:14:51,361
‪This is what I have right now.

1691
01:14:51,445 --> 01:14:53,572
‪-Hey, you'll be safe.
‪-I don't even have two lines.

1692
01:14:53,655 --> 01:14:55,032
‪-No, I'm not.
‪-Come on.

1693
01:14:55,115 --> 01:14:56,950
‪-Not at all.
‪-We still have two rounds left.

1694
01:14:57,034 --> 01:14:58,744
‪There are other people
‪who are worse off than you.

1695
01:14:58,827 --> 01:15:02,498
‪But I'm worried
‪that you'll bid on what I bid

1696
01:15:03,373 --> 01:15:05,584
‪-in Rounds 6 or 7.
‪-I guarantee you won't come in last.

1697
01:15:05,667 --> 01:15:07,169
‪There are people with nothing.

1698
01:15:07,252 --> 01:15:09,546
‪Even if you win this bid,
‪it'd be meaningless.

1699
01:15:09,630 --> 01:15:11,131
‪You should go for these three.

1700
01:15:11,215 --> 01:15:13,258
‪-I was planning to anyway.
‪-There you go.

1701
01:15:13,342 --> 01:15:15,219
‪But what if we bid against each other?

1702
01:15:15,302 --> 01:15:16,345
‪You're worried about me?

1703
01:15:16,428 --> 01:15:18,222
‪If we both go in, I won't be able to win.

1704
01:15:18,305 --> 01:15:21,808
‪But I really can't say yet
‪because I need to see what happens.

1705
01:15:22,643 --> 01:15:26,855
‪Truth be told,
‪I need to play according to my plan.

1706
01:15:26,939 --> 01:15:28,482
‪-You know how I roll.
‪-I do.

1707
01:15:28,565 --> 01:15:31,318
‪I totally respect that,
‪and I'm not asking for intel.

1708
01:15:31,401 --> 01:15:35,197
‪But if you think we're gonna end up
‪bidding against each other,

1709
01:15:35,280 --> 01:15:36,532
‪-can you just let me know?
‪-Right.

1710
01:15:36,615 --> 01:15:39,076
‪Then I can at least use everything I have.

1711
01:15:39,159 --> 01:15:41,245
‪I'll be eliminated
‪if I don't make this happen.

1712
01:15:42,037 --> 01:15:43,205
‪ORBIT.

1713
01:15:43,288 --> 01:15:45,207
‪-Can I just speak to him for a second?
‪-Dong-min.

1714
01:15:45,290 --> 01:15:47,251
‪-I thought you were talking to me.
‪-Give Yurisa something.

1715
01:15:52,381 --> 01:15:55,217
‪Kim Dong-jae, please submit your coins.

1716
01:16:01,098 --> 01:16:04,184
‪I'll bid two or three.
‪Do whatever you want.

1717
01:16:04,977 --> 01:16:06,144
‪Ten seconds remaining.

1718
01:16:08,480 --> 01:16:10,524
‪You have bid one three-won coin.

1719
01:16:10,607 --> 01:16:13,735
‪Now that you're safe,
‪I have to carry out my plan as I said.

1720
01:16:13,819 --> 01:16:16,238
‪After you win this bid,

1721
01:16:16,321 --> 01:16:17,656
‪-I have to play my own game.
‪-Okay.

1722
01:16:17,739 --> 01:16:19,408
‪-Because--
‪-Wait, just listen.

1723
01:16:19,491 --> 01:16:21,368
‪-Going forward--
‪-Okay, okay. I heard you.

1724
01:16:21,451 --> 01:16:22,619
‪Stop taking everything.

1725
01:16:22,703 --> 01:16:26,164
‪I heard you told the others
‪you're bidding seven or eight.

1726
01:16:26,248 --> 01:16:27,249
‪Yeah, I will be.

1727
01:16:27,332 --> 01:16:29,710
‪-Are you really gonna put in that much?
‪-Yeah.

1728
01:16:29,793 --> 01:16:31,795
‪-Must you?
‪-I do.

1729
01:16:31,878 --> 01:16:35,549
‪Because I have to help Yurisa out,
‪and she has a lot of coins right now.

1730
01:16:35,632 --> 01:16:37,217
‪-She barely used any.
‪-That's not true.

1731
01:16:37,301 --> 01:16:40,929
‪If that's why you're doing this,
‪then I can tell you.

1732
01:16:41,013 --> 01:16:42,848
‪She used 19 won on the circles.

1733
01:16:42,931 --> 01:16:44,600
‪-Come on now. Really?
‪-Yeah.

1734
01:16:44,683 --> 01:16:47,185
‪-Then did she win the circles?
‪-Why would I lie to you?

1735
01:16:47,269 --> 01:16:48,270
‪How would I know?

1736
01:16:48,353 --> 01:16:49,896
‪If she spent 19, then she definitely won.

1737
01:16:49,980 --> 01:16:52,065
‪How much did John spend? Did he bid 18?

1738
01:16:53,108 --> 01:16:53,942
‪I'm not sure.

1739
01:16:54,026 --> 01:16:57,154
‪Then John could be in danger
‪if Yurisa won that bid.

1740
01:16:57,237 --> 01:16:58,447
‪She only has four left.

1741
01:16:58,530 --> 01:17:00,866
‪I just can't believe
‪she only has four left.

1742
01:17:00,949 --> 01:17:01,783
‪Listen.

1743
01:17:01,867 --> 01:17:04,494
‪-I swear on everything I have.
‪-So 19 plus 4 equals 23.

1744
01:17:04,578 --> 01:17:05,787
‪-Then I'll leave it to you.
‪-Okay.

1745
01:17:05,871 --> 01:17:09,958
‪I think Yurisa should win this bid
‪with about eight won.

1746
01:17:10,042 --> 01:17:12,544
‪Then go tell her we had this conversation.

1747
01:17:12,628 --> 01:17:14,880
‪Anyway, you're safe now.

1748
01:17:17,466 --> 01:17:19,718
‪It's either Yurisa or me who takes it.

1749
01:17:19,801 --> 01:17:21,428
‪Yurisa has plenty of coins.

1750
01:17:22,054 --> 01:17:22,971
‪You do too, right?

1751
01:17:23,055 --> 01:17:24,556
‪Yes, I have a lot left.

1752
01:17:26,224 --> 01:17:27,643
‪Don't bid one or two.

1753
01:17:27,726 --> 01:17:28,560
‪Definitely not one.

1754
01:17:28,644 --> 01:17:30,437
‪-Why not?
‪-Just because.

1755
01:17:30,520 --> 01:17:31,480
‪I thought it through.

1756
01:17:31,563 --> 01:17:33,231
‪-I don't get it.
‪-That doesn't make sense.

1757
01:17:33,315 --> 01:17:35,817
‪-If we're not gonna win it, why not?
‪-That'd be a waste of our coins.

1758
01:17:35,901 --> 01:17:37,819
<i>‪ORBIT kept sharing </i><i>‪profound </i><i>‪nonsense.</i>

1759
01:17:37,903 --> 01:17:41,448
‪He kept telling me and Kyung-lyul
‪to bid three instead of one or two.

1760
01:17:41,531 --> 01:17:43,116
‪I didn't get why though.

1761
01:17:43,200 --> 01:17:45,661
‪Why is he encouraging us to bid high
‪when either he or Yurisa's gonna take it?

1762
01:17:46,244 --> 01:17:48,246
‪He might be running a mind game,
‪betting you'll go low.

1763
01:17:48,330 --> 01:17:49,873
‪It might just be another mind game.

1764
01:17:49,956 --> 01:17:52,459
‪No, he wouldn't lie about that.

1765
01:17:52,542 --> 01:17:55,754
‪-Really?
‪-Yeah, just bid less. Bid one.

1766
01:17:55,837 --> 01:17:57,422
‪-I'm gonna bid one.
‪-I'll bid two.

1767
01:17:57,506 --> 01:17:59,841
‪But she'll be in trouble
‪if she doesn't win anything.

1768
01:17:59,925 --> 01:18:01,259
‪That can't be helped.

1769
01:18:01,343 --> 01:18:03,136
‪You can't run out of coins yet.

1770
01:18:03,220 --> 01:18:05,555
‪You need to save it for that one chance.

1771
01:18:08,225 --> 01:18:10,519
‪-Nine to be safe.
‪-Okay.

1772
01:18:10,602 --> 01:18:12,062
‪-Go ahead and make your bid.
‪-Okay.

1773
01:18:13,313 --> 01:18:14,272
‪-Me first?
‪-Yeah.

1774
01:18:16,525 --> 01:18:19,111
‪-ORBIT, please submit your coins.
‪-Okay.

1775
01:18:21,947 --> 01:18:22,906
‪-Nine, right?
‪-Right.

1776
01:18:22,989 --> 01:18:24,616
‪-I'll bid ten.
‪-Okay.

1777
01:18:25,701 --> 01:18:26,910
‪Please submit your coins.

1778
01:18:28,620 --> 01:18:30,163
‪One one-won coin.

1779
01:18:30,247 --> 01:18:31,748
‪I'll bid one won.

1780
01:18:32,708 --> 01:18:35,043
‪You have bid one one-won coin.

1781
01:18:35,127 --> 01:18:36,253
‪I'm the only one, right?

1782
01:18:36,336 --> 01:18:37,671
‪No other bidders on the circle, right?

1783
01:18:37,754 --> 01:18:39,089
‪I cannot disclose that.

1784
01:18:39,172 --> 01:18:40,924
‪-Then can I step outside?
‪-You cannot.

1785
01:18:41,007 --> 01:18:43,927
‪Damn it. Then I should do 10.
‪No, 11 to be safe.

1786
01:18:45,887 --> 01:18:47,764
<i>‪Bidding is now complete.</i>

1787
01:18:47,848 --> 01:18:50,851
<i>‪Here is the winning bid for each shape.</i>

1788
01:18:50,934 --> 01:18:54,312
‪△: 2 WON, ◯: 1 WON, ☆: SECRET

1789
01:18:54,396 --> 01:18:55,772
‪What?

1790
01:18:55,856 --> 01:18:57,524
‪Well, that's a flop.

1791
01:18:57,607 --> 01:18:58,900
‪What the hell?

1792
01:18:59,609 --> 01:19:00,861
‪Yurisa, are you really out of coins?

1793
01:19:00,944 --> 01:19:02,112
‪He told you.

1794
01:19:03,071 --> 01:19:04,698
‪I guess she really is.

1795
01:19:04,781 --> 01:19:08,493
‪Do you really think you're someone
‪who can speak things into existence?

1796
01:19:08,577 --> 01:19:10,120
‪I asked you so nicely, didn't I?

1797
01:19:10,704 --> 01:19:12,581
‪She told me she had a lot.

1798
01:19:12,664 --> 01:19:14,374
‪I told you she didn't.

1799
01:19:14,458 --> 01:19:15,959
<i>‪Round 6 will now begin.</i>

1800
01:19:16,460 --> 01:19:18,795
<i>‪Please select your shape.</i>

1801
01:19:19,671 --> 01:19:21,256
‪You go first in Round 6.

1802
01:19:23,550 --> 01:19:24,843
‪Help the ones who don't have anything.

1803
01:19:24,926 --> 01:19:26,428
‪Why did you lie to me?

1804
01:19:26,511 --> 01:19:28,221
‪-What did I lie about?
‪-You said you'd bid eight.

1805
01:19:28,305 --> 01:19:30,348
‪Why did you lie and say you'd bid eight?

1806
01:19:30,432 --> 01:19:32,517
‪-I just wanted to check.
‪-I told my team…

1807
01:19:33,018 --> 01:19:35,353
‪So when you do it, it's checking,

1808
01:19:36,188 --> 01:19:37,939
‪-but when others do it, it's lying?
‪-Just leave.

1809
01:19:38,023 --> 01:19:39,733
‪-I apologize for lying.
‪-Tell me.

1810
01:19:39,816 --> 01:19:42,402
‪-Hey.
‪-I bid one and not eight. My apologies.

1811
01:19:42,486 --> 01:19:44,446
‪You bid one? Don't lie. You bid two.

1812
01:19:44,529 --> 01:19:45,781
‪-You bid two.
‪-He bid one.

1813
01:19:45,864 --> 01:19:46,698
‪I bid one.

1814
01:19:46,782 --> 01:19:48,283
‪He bid one, leaving Kyung-lyul to win.

1815
01:19:48,366 --> 01:19:50,827
‪-Then why would I pick the triangle again?
‪-He went for the triangle.

1816
01:19:50,911 --> 01:19:52,954
‪If I had won it,
‪I have no reason to do that.

1817
01:19:53,038 --> 01:19:54,831
‪-Hold on a minute.
‪-This is so confusing.

1818
01:19:54,915 --> 01:19:55,832
‪-Did I bid two?
‪-Why would I…

1819
01:20:00,420 --> 01:20:02,380
‪You have bid one two-won coin.

1820
01:20:02,464 --> 01:20:03,924
‪Thank you.

1821
01:20:04,007 --> 01:20:05,926
‪-He didn't even need it.
‪-I just grabbed a small coin.

1822
01:20:06,009 --> 01:20:07,719
‪-You…
‪-Seriously.

1823
01:20:07,803 --> 01:20:10,555
‪It'd be better if ORBIT weren't here.
‪He's driving me nuts.

1824
01:20:10,639 --> 01:20:12,599
‪-He just keeps spewing nonsense.
‪-I apologize.

1825
01:20:12,682 --> 01:20:14,142
‪-I mean, 95% of what he says is nonsense.
‪-ORBIT.

1826
01:20:14,226 --> 01:20:16,520
‪-Sorry about that.
‪-Your gameplay isn't scientific at all.

1827
01:20:16,603 --> 01:20:18,188
‪I couldn't observe it
‪before I submitted it.

1828
01:20:18,271 --> 01:20:21,024
‪-What, because of quantum mechanics?
‪-Yeah, it just sort of happened.

1829
01:20:21,107 --> 01:20:23,568
‪I don't even know who you are anymore.
‪You're something else.

1830
01:20:23,652 --> 01:20:26,029
‪If I don't lie here,

1831
01:20:26,655 --> 01:20:28,448
‪the game would be too dull.

1832
01:20:28,532 --> 01:20:29,533
‪You know,

1833
01:20:30,283 --> 01:20:32,452
‪I guess ORBIT's reputation
‪just blinded all of us.

1834
01:20:32,536 --> 01:20:34,246
‪I really thought
‪he wasn't the type to betray someone.

1835
01:20:34,329 --> 01:20:37,415
‪Yeah, he just helps out whoever's losing.

1836
01:20:37,499 --> 01:20:40,335
‪-You absolutely have to negotiate.
‪-I need to win the circle bid.

1837
01:20:40,418 --> 01:20:44,923
‪The circle bid is gonna be chaos
‪because of Dong-min.

1838
01:20:45,006 --> 01:20:47,717
‪So you should go
‪for the triangle or the star.

1839
01:20:47,801 --> 01:20:49,594
‪Go for the triangle or the star.

1840
01:20:49,678 --> 01:20:51,596
‪Select wherever there are fewer people

1841
01:20:51,680 --> 01:20:53,557
‪and then make a deal.

1842
01:20:53,640 --> 01:20:55,058
‪That'd give you the best chance.

1843
01:20:55,141 --> 01:20:55,976
‪But I already chose.

1844
01:20:56,059 --> 01:20:57,769
‪You should be out there,
‪watching what they choose.

1845
01:20:57,853 --> 01:20:58,687
‪I already chose the circle.

1846
01:20:58,770 --> 01:21:00,063
‪-You did?
‪-Yes.

1847
01:21:00,647 --> 01:21:02,440
‪Why is everyone going for the circle?
‪This is nuts.

1848
01:21:02,524 --> 01:21:04,025
‪Because not many won them.

1849
01:21:04,109 --> 01:21:06,027
‪We can't have everyone
‪bidding for the circle.

1850
01:21:11,741 --> 01:21:13,869
‪A lot of people
‪are going for the circle this round.

1851
01:21:13,952 --> 01:21:15,537
‪Dong-min could end up taking it.

1852
01:21:15,620 --> 01:21:17,372
‪He already has one and needs three more.

1853
01:21:17,455 --> 01:21:20,542
‪I can only block him once,

1854
01:21:20,625 --> 01:21:22,168
‪either in Round 6 or 7.

1855
01:21:22,252 --> 01:21:25,922
‪He's gonna bid on what I bid
‪and just go all in to block me.

1856
01:21:30,677 --> 01:21:32,012
‪ORBIT chose the circle.

1857
01:21:32,512 --> 01:21:33,972
‪I have no other choice.

1858
01:21:35,640 --> 01:21:37,267
‪-What are you choosing?
‪-Go for the circle.

1859
01:21:37,851 --> 01:21:38,977
‪Okay, take the star.

1860
01:21:40,645 --> 01:21:42,647
<i>‪Shape selection is now closed.</i>

1861
01:21:42,731 --> 01:21:45,734
<i>‪Here are the shapes</i>
<i>‪each player has selected.</i>

1862
01:21:47,944 --> 01:21:49,237
‪Yurisa got one.

1863
01:21:49,321 --> 01:21:51,156
‪That's great.
‪She can put the star in the middle.

1864
01:21:51,656 --> 01:21:53,742
<i>‪Bidding will now begin.</i>

1865
01:21:53,825 --> 01:21:57,537
<i>‪Triangle, triangle, </i><i>‪triangle</i>
<i>‪Triangle, </i><i>‪triangle, </i><i>‪triangle</i>

1866
01:21:58,830 --> 01:22:01,958
<i>‪Triangle, triangle, </i><i>‪triangle</i>
<i>‪Triangle, </i><i>‪triangle</i>

1867
01:22:02,042 --> 01:22:03,585
‪Should we hold back a bit?

1868
01:22:03,668 --> 01:22:04,961
‪Oh boy.

1869
01:22:05,045 --> 01:22:07,005
‪What are you thinking?

1870
01:22:09,049 --> 01:22:12,427
‪How many triangles do you have right now?

1871
01:22:12,510 --> 01:22:16,431
‪I hope you can trust me when I say this,
‪but I only need one.

1872
01:22:16,514 --> 01:22:18,767
‪How much do you think
‪it'll take for us to make a deal?

1873
01:22:18,850 --> 01:22:20,769
‪One at this point would never happen.

1874
01:22:20,852 --> 01:22:24,314
‪But this is more of a trust thing.
‪How many do you need? Be honest.

1875
01:22:24,397 --> 01:22:25,482
‪I could use all of them.

1876
01:22:25,565 --> 01:22:27,275
‪That might be difficult.

1877
01:22:27,359 --> 01:22:30,195
‪I just need one.

1878
01:22:30,278 --> 01:22:32,864
‪But just one would be fine too.

1879
01:22:32,948 --> 01:22:34,282
‪Should we go for it?

1880
01:22:34,366 --> 01:22:36,117
‪I'll bid all of it.

1881
01:22:36,201 --> 01:22:38,119
‪Please verify what you're submitting.

1882
01:22:38,203 --> 01:22:41,414
‪One five-won coin,
‪two two-won coins, two one-won coins.

1883
01:22:41,498 --> 01:22:43,041
‪I'll bid six won.

1884
01:22:46,461 --> 01:22:49,506
‪You have bid one two-won coin.

1885
01:22:50,090 --> 01:22:51,257
‪Are you looking to win?

1886
01:22:51,341 --> 01:22:53,551
‪Taking the circle in the next round
‪would be meaningless for me

1887
01:22:53,635 --> 01:22:55,095
‪if there aren't enough people.

1888
01:22:55,178 --> 01:22:57,347
‪I'll leave one behind and bid the rest.

1889
01:22:57,430 --> 01:22:59,057
‪Will seven be enough?

1890
01:23:02,852 --> 01:23:06,189
‪ORBIT's plan is to go down
‪after burning everything

1891
01:23:06,272 --> 01:23:07,315
‪-to get me.
‪-Right.

1892
01:23:07,399 --> 01:23:10,110
‪He's been biding his time to dump it all
‪into one of these rounds.

1893
01:23:10,193 --> 01:23:11,194
‪-You know that, right?
‪-Yes.

1894
01:23:11,277 --> 01:23:14,030
‪He bid one won every time,
‪except once when it was two won.

1895
01:23:14,114 --> 01:23:15,573
‪There's no way I can beat him.

1896
01:23:15,657 --> 01:23:18,368
‪-Still, we can't go head-to-head now.
‪-Right.

1897
01:23:18,952 --> 01:23:22,247
‪-If you manage to win all four this round,
‪-Yes?

1898
01:23:22,330 --> 01:23:23,915
‪-will it fill your board?
‪-No.

1899
01:23:28,253 --> 01:23:30,422
‪ORBIT, please help me out.

1900
01:23:30,505 --> 01:23:32,090
‪-Yurisa, can we have the room?
‪-Okay.

1901
01:23:32,173 --> 01:23:33,425
‪Jeez, Dong-jae.

1902
01:23:33,508 --> 01:23:35,468
‪Yurisa has nothing right now.

1903
01:23:35,552 --> 01:23:37,220
‪I just have one star. Or I will soon.

1904
01:23:38,179 --> 01:23:42,267
‪-If Yurisa's in last place, you're safe.
‪-You won't be eliminated.

1905
01:23:42,892 --> 01:23:45,562
‪-Why so serious?
‪-We both know that's not true.

1906
01:23:45,645 --> 01:23:46,688
‪Why is she so relaxed?

1907
01:23:46,771 --> 01:23:48,064
‪-ORBIT.
‪-She might've won triangles.

1908
01:23:48,148 --> 01:23:49,315
‪You know that's not true.

1909
01:23:49,399 --> 01:23:51,943
‪-Do you have one star?
‪-Yes.

1910
01:23:52,027 --> 01:23:55,405
‪You should've gone for the star
‪and made a deal with Yurisa.

1911
01:23:55,488 --> 01:23:56,656
‪What are you gonna bid on?

1912
01:23:56,740 --> 01:23:57,782
‪-In the next round?
‪-Yes.

1913
01:23:57,866 --> 01:24:00,452
‪-Well, I'll need to…
‪-You need to think about it?

1914
01:24:00,535 --> 01:24:02,996
‪I do, but it should be fun.

1915
01:24:03,079 --> 01:24:04,789
‪How so? Are you going all in?

1916
01:24:05,540 --> 01:24:06,583
‪Yeah.

1917
01:24:06,666 --> 01:24:09,461
‪But either way,
‪nobody can touch me next round.

1918
01:24:09,544 --> 01:24:13,256
‪So you should avoid me.

1919
01:24:13,339 --> 01:24:16,176
‪How can I when I don't know
‪what you'll be choosing?

1920
01:24:16,259 --> 01:24:17,635
‪That's true.

1921
01:24:18,636 --> 01:24:20,805
‪You should find out by today.

1922
01:24:23,099 --> 01:24:24,225
‪Seriously.

1923
01:24:24,309 --> 01:24:27,312
‪ORBIT's got a lot of coins right now.

1924
01:24:27,395 --> 01:24:29,230
‪He's been biding for one big shot,

1925
01:24:29,314 --> 01:24:30,857
‪so he's definitely gonna take that one.

1926
01:24:30,940 --> 01:24:35,236
‪Some people would've anticipated that
‪and saved their coins for the circles.

1927
01:24:35,320 --> 01:24:37,822
‪-Hoping to see chaos?
‪-Yeah.

1928
01:24:39,324 --> 01:24:40,533
‪Please submit your coins.

1929
01:24:40,617 --> 01:24:41,785
‪Okay.

1930
01:24:44,871 --> 01:24:45,955
‪ORBIT.

1931
01:24:47,248 --> 01:24:50,585
‪You need to tell me the truth this time.

1932
01:24:50,668 --> 01:24:52,545
‪-About the last round?
‪-What?

1933
01:24:52,629 --> 01:24:53,922
‪No, this round.

1934
01:24:54,005 --> 01:24:56,424
‪Everyone's saying they're gonna go all in.

1935
01:24:56,508 --> 01:24:58,927
‪-Right, so…
‪-You will too, right?

1936
01:24:59,010 --> 01:25:00,136
‪-So tell me.
‪-Yes?

1937
01:25:00,220 --> 01:25:01,429
‪What did you do?

1938
01:25:01,513 --> 01:25:02,347
‪Me?

1939
01:25:02,430 --> 01:25:05,100
‪How can I when everyone else is?
‪I still have one more round.

1940
01:25:07,018 --> 01:25:08,186
‪I still have the last round.

1941
01:25:09,187 --> 01:25:10,647
‪-You mean that?
‪-Yeah.

1942
01:25:10,730 --> 01:25:11,898
‪-Really?
‪-I have the last round.

1943
01:25:11,981 --> 01:25:14,150
‪I have an excellent idea
‪for the final round.

1944
01:25:14,901 --> 01:25:16,027
‪You'll be shocked.

1945
01:25:16,111 --> 01:25:19,823
‪We still have one more round.
‪I'm sure you'll be fine with the results.

1946
01:25:19,906 --> 01:25:21,741
<i>‪If I were ORBIT, I'd blow up Round 7 too.</i>

1947
01:25:21,825 --> 01:25:24,160
‪If I go all in during Round 6,

1948
01:25:24,244 --> 01:25:25,703
<i>‪I'll be fine.</i>

1949
01:25:25,787 --> 01:25:28,581
<i>‪If I'm lucky, I can even fill my board.</i>

1950
01:25:28,665 --> 01:25:31,709
‪But there's one issue.

1951
01:25:31,793 --> 01:25:33,128
‪Then I'll just…

1952
01:25:33,753 --> 01:25:35,547
‪-I'll just do what we talked about.
‪-What?

1953
01:25:35,630 --> 01:25:38,716
‪-Just hold on a second.
‪-Okay, go ahead.

1954
01:25:38,800 --> 01:25:41,970
‪Dong-jae has fewer coins than I do,

1955
01:25:42,053 --> 01:25:43,763
‪and he needs the circles too.

1956
01:25:43,847 --> 01:25:48,476
<i>‪I'm well aware</i>
<i>‪that </i><i>‪he's </i><i>‪desperate </i><i>‪for </i><i>‪them.</i>

1957
01:25:48,560 --> 01:25:52,480
‪I can't just turn my back on him
‪because I can outbid him anyway.

1958
01:25:56,234 --> 01:25:57,402
‪I just couldn't.

1959
01:25:57,485 --> 01:25:59,988
‪-I'll let you take it.
‪-What do you mean?

1960
01:26:00,071 --> 01:26:02,323
‪ORBIT said he's going all in next round,
‪not now.

1961
01:26:02,407 --> 01:26:04,576
‪-Then why are you doing this?
‪-You take it.

1962
01:26:04,659 --> 01:26:05,660
‪-I don't understand.
‪-What?

1963
01:26:05,743 --> 01:26:08,121
‪-It's okay. Go on.
‪-Then you'll be eliminated.

1964
01:26:08,788 --> 01:26:10,623
‪It's fine.

1965
01:26:10,707 --> 01:26:11,541
‪Go for it.

1966
01:26:11,624 --> 01:26:12,876
‪No, that's not right.

1967
01:26:12,959 --> 01:26:14,627
‪-Just hurry up.
‪-That can't happen.

1968
01:26:14,711 --> 01:26:15,753
‪Just go already.

1969
01:26:15,837 --> 01:26:17,422
‪I'm gonna bid one.

1970
01:26:17,505 --> 01:26:20,967
<i>‪As long as I'm not in last place,</i>
<i>‪I'll make it to the prison match.</i>

1971
01:26:21,050 --> 01:26:23,803
‪I just need to make it back alive.

1972
01:26:23,887 --> 01:26:25,054
‪But it didn't feel right…

1973
01:26:26,431 --> 01:26:28,558
‪to hand over such a burden to Dong-jae.

1974
01:26:29,601 --> 01:26:31,060
‪Please submit your coins.

1975
01:26:32,061 --> 01:26:34,898
‪I don't know anymore.

1976
01:26:35,523 --> 01:26:39,152
‪Two one-won coins, two two-won coins,
‪and one ten-won coin.

1977
01:26:39,777 --> 01:26:41,571
‪Creators of <i>‪The Devil's Plan,</i>

1978
01:26:41,654 --> 01:26:43,072
‪you guys did well this season.

1979
01:26:44,866 --> 01:26:46,492
‪He's running his own interview.

1980
01:26:46,576 --> 01:26:49,412
‪You even managed to shake me to the core.

1981
01:26:50,622 --> 01:26:51,789
‪I have to hand it to you all.

1982
01:26:51,873 --> 01:26:53,249
‪I'll use a Piece.

1983
01:26:53,333 --> 01:26:54,667
‪-Would you like to exchange your Piece?
‪-Yes.

1984
01:26:54,751 --> 01:26:57,712
‪You have exchanged one Piece for one won.

1985
01:27:03,801 --> 01:27:05,887
‪You have bid one one-won coin.

1986
01:27:06,387 --> 01:27:08,181
<i>‪Bidding is now complete.</i>

1987
01:27:08,973 --> 01:27:12,018
<i>‪Here is the winning bid for each shape.</i>

1988
01:27:12,101 --> 01:27:14,103
‪△: 11 WON, ◯: SECRET, ☆: 1 WON

1989
01:27:14,187 --> 01:27:15,730
‪Someone won it for 11 won.

1990
01:27:15,813 --> 01:27:17,982
‪Wow, there's still a lot of money around.

1991
01:27:18,733 --> 01:27:20,693
<i>‪Round 7 will now begin.</i>

1992
01:27:23,821 --> 01:27:24,948
‪Hold on.

1993
01:27:25,031 --> 01:27:26,824
‪You need to choose carefully.

1994
01:27:29,244 --> 01:27:31,871
‪Let's see what people choose.

1995
01:27:32,372 --> 01:27:35,166
‪We can end up helping people

1996
01:27:35,250 --> 01:27:37,627
‪who desperately need a certain shape.

1997
01:27:37,710 --> 01:27:41,798
‪For example, if ORBIT had won Round 6,
‪Dong-min couldn't have gotten the circles.

1998
01:27:41,881 --> 01:27:43,591
‪-He'd only have one circle then.
‪-Right.

1999
01:27:43,675 --> 01:27:45,760
‪-So he'll go for the circle again.
‪-Right.

2000
01:27:45,843 --> 01:27:50,348
‪-It'd be better to limit circle bidders.
‪-We should all go for the triangle.

2001
01:27:51,015 --> 01:27:53,142
‪If we go for the circle,
‪we'd only be helping him out.

2002
01:27:53,226 --> 01:27:55,019
‪So you have to think carefully here.

2003
01:27:55,103 --> 01:27:56,813
‪-It'd be better to avoid the circle.
‪-Right.

2004
01:27:56,896 --> 01:28:00,024
‪-Do you have one coin left now?
‪-Yes.

2005
01:28:00,108 --> 01:28:01,317
‪What about you?

2006
01:28:01,401 --> 01:28:02,235
‪One?

2007
01:28:02,318 --> 01:28:03,653
‪-And you?
‪-Coins?

2008
01:28:03,736 --> 01:28:04,654
‪Yeah. Do you have any?

2009
01:28:04,737 --> 01:28:06,364
‪Then you stay put.

2010
01:28:07,782 --> 01:28:08,741
‪Okay.

2011
01:28:08,825 --> 01:28:11,119
‪I'll ask Yurisa whether she's going
‪for the circle or the triangle.

2012
01:28:11,202 --> 01:28:13,204
‪-I really need to help her out.
‪-Okay.

2013
01:28:13,705 --> 01:28:16,624
‪Then just go in as late as possible.

2014
01:28:16,708 --> 01:28:19,502
‪And you can do what I asked, right?

2015
01:28:19,585 --> 01:28:22,088
‪-I really wanna help you because I'm done.
‪-Okay.

2016
01:28:22,171 --> 01:28:25,258
‪Whatever you choose, I'll do the same
‪and help you take at least one more.

2017
01:28:25,341 --> 01:28:29,470
‪I went all in earlier
‪and bid 11 won to win the triangles.

2018
01:28:29,554 --> 01:28:30,847
‪I'm all set now.

2019
01:28:30,930 --> 01:28:32,015
‪-You're done?
‪-I'm out of coins.

2020
01:28:32,098 --> 01:28:33,599
‪-How much do you have?
‪-I have nothing.

2021
01:28:33,683 --> 01:28:35,810
<i>‪For me, the last round will come down to</i>

2022
01:28:35,893 --> 01:28:39,814
‪whether or not I can win the triangles
‪with my seven-won bid.

2023
01:28:39,897 --> 01:28:43,693
‪If I can't get them, I could end up
‪near the bottom of the rankings.

2024
01:28:43,776 --> 01:28:45,653
‪I really wanna help
‪because I have nothing.

2025
01:28:45,737 --> 01:28:47,613
‪Okay. Let's see what happens.

2026
01:28:47,697 --> 01:28:51,159
‪I think I'll go for the star.
‪I still need one.

2027
01:28:51,242 --> 01:28:53,911
‪Well, it doesn't matter much either way.

2028
01:28:54,579 --> 01:28:55,663
‪I'll be going to prison.

2029
01:28:55,747 --> 01:28:57,081
‪Did everyone go?

2030
01:28:57,165 --> 01:28:58,750
‪Did you all go?

2031
01:28:58,833 --> 01:29:03,963
‪If ORBIT goes for the star,
‪that means he's going for first.

2032
01:29:04,047 --> 01:29:04,881
‪Let's see.

2033
01:29:04,964 --> 01:29:07,008
‪-He's also looking to win first place?
‪-Yeah.

2034
01:29:07,091 --> 01:29:08,009
‪What should I choose?

2035
01:29:08,092 --> 01:29:09,510
‪Do you have a preference?

2036
01:29:10,345 --> 01:29:12,180
‪-You're going for the star, right?
‪-All right.

2037
01:29:13,556 --> 01:29:14,932
‪Here we go.

2038
01:29:15,558 --> 01:29:17,393
‪I don't know what I'll be bidding on.

2039
01:29:18,269 --> 01:29:20,521
‪-There.
‪-Is this allowed?

2040
01:29:20,605 --> 01:29:21,439
‪What?

2041
01:29:22,231 --> 01:29:23,775
‪-I'm done.
‪-Are you kidding me?

2042
01:29:23,858 --> 01:29:25,443
‪I'll stop all communications.

2043
01:29:26,361 --> 01:29:27,779
‪Can you even do that?

2044
01:29:27,862 --> 01:29:29,197
‪Who went? What did ORBIT choose?

2045
01:29:29,781 --> 01:29:30,698
‪-The star?
‪-It's a secret.

2046
01:29:30,782 --> 01:29:33,493
‪I actually don't know either.

2047
01:29:34,077 --> 01:29:35,453
‪Can I put in something besides a ticket?

2048
01:29:35,536 --> 01:29:38,748
‪You may put in something else,
‪but you must not touch the ballot box.

2049
01:29:42,085 --> 01:29:44,754
‪-I don't know what I'll be bidding on.
‪-What?

2050
01:29:44,837 --> 01:29:46,047
‪-There.
‪-Is this allowed?

2051
01:29:46,130 --> 01:29:47,757
‪You really are something else.

2052
01:31:27,398 --> 01:31:32,403
‪Subtitle translation by: Justin S. Kim
